{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/498162-second-edition-darklings","id":498162,"title":"Second Edition Darklings.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-04-30T20:30:58-07:00","id":498162,"title":"Second Edition Darklings.","content":"Here's the thread to talk about them.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/changeling-the-lost-second-edition-darklings/\" target=\"_blank\">You can find the first draft here. </a><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":70,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","user":"MachineIV","date":". 04-30-2015, 11:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-30T20:42:06-07:00","id":498212,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Curse: A Shade\u2019s Distrust. A Darkling has been injured in the past, and believes she\u2019s injured others to survive. A Darkling trusted once, a long time ago, and anyone asking her to trust may be pushing her too hard. Trusting anyone, even a Darklings\u2019 closest allies, following them blindly, causes the Darkling to suffer a Clarity break. </span></span></span> </div> </div> </div>This curse I see as being someone problematic in what is supposed to be a team game. A Darkling PC spending thirty minutes of game time establishing that they're going along with the plan without any trust at all every single time anything happens could get really annoying. I think it would be best to narrow the focus a bit rather than leaving it so open ended.<br /> <br /> [edit]Maybe clarify the level of trust? Trusting that the Ogre will go smash faces while you execute your part of the plan is a much lesser degree of trust than allowing the Fairest to leave you behind because &quot;trust me, I'll be back to rescue you.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":2757,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","user":"proindrakenzol","date":". 04-30-2015, 11:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-30T20:47:48-07:00","id":498215,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/498162-second-edition-darklings?p=498212#post498212\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This curse I see as being someone problematic in what is supposed to be a team game. A Darkling PC spending thirty minutes of game time establishing that they're going along with the plan without any trust at all every single time anything happens could get really annoying. I think it would be best to narrow the focus a bit rather than leaving it so open ended.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll clarify in the later draft. The point is, blindly following is the problem. Not having a Plan B. Not paying attention to exits. Putting your safety solely in someone else's hands. Fundamental, deep trust.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-30T20:54:49-07:00","id":498249,"title":"","content":"I'm gonna say it... Excellent write-up, completely unexpected but totally makes sense. I however now have a disliking for the Darklings, not for anything bad in the write-up, no... Just for what they stand for now... Workaholics that step whoever's in the way to get forward in life. Yeesh.<br /> <br /> Still, I can see stories to be told there. I wonder how their hero, the one who abandoned them when they escaped their own Durance would think of their old comrade when they meet in Reality? That is an interesting story I'd like to see. The Face-Heel turn of what they are is something interesting too. I think playing through a Prologue where the Darkling is a mortal before being snatched up and leading to their Escape could be very rewarding.<br /> <br /> As an aside, I noticed a slight potential typo in describing their appearance around the 'hair in eyes' part. I don't know if it was intentional though it says 'hair in hair in'.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3951-wander","name":"wander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"409"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-30T20:57:23-07:00","id":498250,"title":"","content":"Damn, this is good stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: the Ascension - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1191028-redesigned-prime-sphere\" target=\"_blank\">Redesigned Prime Sphere</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188769-simpler-wonder-creation\" target=\"_blank\">Streamlined Wonder Creation</a><br /> Mummy: the Curse - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/474927-mummy-the-curse-2e-conversion\" target=\"_blank\">Lightweight 2E Conversion</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/22378-second-sight-tradition-disciples-of-duat\" target=\"_blank\">Disciples of Duat</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/61-octavo","name":"Octavo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar61_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-30T21:13:57-07:00","id":498257,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/498162-second-edition-darklings?p=498249#post498249\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm gonna say it... Excellent write-up, completely unexpected but totally makes sense. I however now have a disliking for the Darklings, not for anything bad in the write-up, no... Just for what they stand for now... Workaholics that step whoever's in the way to get forward in life. Yeesh.<br /> <br /> Still, I can see stories to be told there. I wonder how their hero, the one who abandoned them when they escaped their own Durance would think of their old comrade when they meet in Reality? That is an interesting story I'd like to see. The Face-Heel turn of what they are is something interesting too. I think playing through a Prologue where the Darkling is a mortal before being snatched up and leading to their Escape could be very rewarding.<br /> <br /> As an aside, I noticed a slight potential typo in describing their appearance around the 'hair in eyes' part. I don't know if it was intentional though it says 'hair in hair in'.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, just a typo. <br /> <br /> And despite the dislike, I find your take really positive. Thank you. I think I might struggle to play them, too. But I definitely have people in my crew that will love them that way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-30T21:39:41-07:00","id":498274,"title":"","content":"This write-up so vividly describes my first Darkling character that it's uncanny.<br /> <br /> This is fantastic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-30T21:39:55-07:00","id":498275,"title":"","content":"I like it a lot. Seemings have drama built in, it seems, and Darklings ask some hard things that make for delicious conflict.<br /> <br /> Another thing I like, less on the trauma subext of Changeling and more on the psychological aspect, is how the Seemings seem to be partly about confronting things about the individual that holding them back as much as anything in Arcadia. It's a dangerous maturation to make, but it's also an important one, to learn when things in our lives are boons and structures that build us up and when they become chains that bind us in our own dramas and nightmares.<br /> <br /> I'm becoming more and more, as I go along, a person who favors morality over practicality, but <i>man</i> do I sympathize with the Darklings on that subject.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Crap, actually, I <i>would</i> be one of these if I were a changeling, if we go off of the Blessing. I am <i>constantly</i> being the one who makes those decisions in my apartment.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 05-01-2015, 12:48 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-30T22:02:46-07:00","id":498292,"title":"","content":"Themes of abandonment and isolation in conjunction with Bloody-Minded Pragmatism and amorality.<br /> <br /> &lt;Sigh&gt;<br /> <br /> I'll add that to the pile of reasons I should play a darkling.<br /> <br /> (Seriously, though, this is exactly the sort of thing I like to play.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/526-schizopop","name":"schizoPOP","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"108"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-30T22:36:18-07:00","id":498322,"title":"","content":"Whelp, they were already my favorite Seeming.<br /> <br /> Now they are even more my favorite Seeming.<br /> <br /> Darkling Ifrit, here I come (<i>a dread looming shape, dripping pitch and ash; her eyes are eternally-dying embers</i>)<br /> <br /> Burning what needs to be burned.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-30T22:38:36-07:00","id":498323,"title":"","content":"Doesnt the introduction contradicts the way of the Darkling??<br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i><span style=\"font-size:15px\">I will follow you to the end of the earth if I must, but please, please, don\u2019t ever turn your back to me.</span></i></span></span><br /> That sounds a lot like blind trust.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1351-sakii","name":"Sakii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1351_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-30T22:39:48-07:00","id":498326,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sakii</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/498162-second-edition-darklings?p=498323#post498323\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Doesnt the introduction contradicts the way of the Darkling??<br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i><span style=\"font-size:15px\">I will follow you to the end of the earth if I must, but please, please, don\u2019t ever turn your back to me.</span></i></span></span><br /> That sounds a lot like blind trust.<br /> <br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Ironically, that's not the quote that's in the current draft. That was a placeholder.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-30T23:05:03-07:00","id":498357,"title":"","content":"I rather liked the placeholder quote, but maybe because I interpreted it as coming from someone who sees themselves as the scorpion in the fable of the scorpion and the frog. They're pleading someone they care for not to turn their back, because the Darkling can't trust themselves not to stab the person they're pleading with in the back.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2286-indarkestknight","name":"indarkestknight","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"53"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-30T23:24:26-07:00","id":498395,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>indarkestknight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/498162-second-edition-darklings?p=498357#post498357\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I rather liked the placeholder quote, but maybe because I interpreted it as coming from someone who sees themselves as the scorpion in the fable of the scorpion and the frog. They're pleading someone they care for not to turn their back, because the Darkling can't trust themselves not to stab the person they're pleading with in the back.</div> </div> </div> </div>That was the idea, more or less. But, we settled on a slightly different convention for these quotes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-30T23:29:52-07:00","id":498398,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/498162-second-edition-darklings?p=498215#post498215\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'll clarify in the later draft. The point is, blindly following is the problem. Not having a Plan B. Not paying attention to exits. Putting your safety solely in someone else's hands. Fundamental, deep trust.</div> </div> </div> </div>What about a Pledge? If you want to have a game about foiling a loyalist's dasterdly plot, or about establishing your new life with the Motley as a self-help group - could you say that if eveyone has a Pledge the Darkling doesn't need trust and avoids the curse?<br /> <br /> [edit]<br /> <br /> Having read it, I feel that this draft is far far too specific.<br /> <br /> This didn't read like a splat to me, but almost like one specific if rather cool charachter.<br /> <br /> Lets start with the Background - to me it read as &quot;All Darklings were loyal people in life&quot;. However you become a Darkling by betraying someone in order to escape.<br /> <br /> A powerfully loyal person - like the housewife example in this write up - who betrays someone in order to escape Arcadia is a cool story. But what about the housewife's opposite, someone who marries just for the divorce settlement. Put them in Arcadia and it's likely they'll become a Darkling because creating false loyalty then betraying for self benefit is their modus operandi.<br /> <br /> I think it's important that any charachter can become any Seeming depending on their Durance, to the point that I'm not sure there even should be a section on their pre-Durance life.<br /> <br /> <br /> Moving on to The Escape - same issue. It's too specific. It puts a single event and says it's common to every Darkling's backstory. That event being that someone else abandoned them. I just don't think that should be the case. A Darkling could be someone who decided from day one that they'd do anything, and when the opportunity arose they did something terrible. Or maybe it was the Keeper just one day offered freedom if they betrayed another to changeling who was loyal to their fellow slaves and never doubted that loyalty in return, but the changeling made the snap decision to accept.<br /> <br /> I think this section would be much improved if you just simply cut out the beginning and started with the sentence &quot;she did what she had to do to escape&quot;. Remove everything before that, keep everything afterwords, and it would be great.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 05-01-2015, 02:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-01T01:28:48-07:00","id":498493,"title":"","content":"Overly, I love it, but I think the language, ironically, could do with a bit of loosening up. What about if being betrayed <i>during</i> the Escape and getting through regardless is another way of becoming a Darkling?<br /> <br /> As for the Curse, I think having something more along the lines of the Beasts wouldn't be a bad idea - the Darkling's trusting Clarity Break is a once per story thing, and they have a minor mechanical disadvantage along with that, rather than the 'every time I truly trust someone'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/209-that-other-guy","name":"That Other Guy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-01T01:45:24-07:00","id":498497,"title":"","content":"One of the character concepts makes me curious though, the one about the scholar into the occult looking into demonology, necromancy, fetishism, etc? <br /> <br /> Other than demonology that can be learned by anyone, ala Inferno, are contracts going to be versatile enough to cover such things? <br /> <br /> The academic study of something you can't actually use doesn't seem to be the darkling thing, they learn obscure forbidden arts to use them, to make a point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-01T02:06:42-07:00","id":498507,"title":"","content":"I guess I felt it was a little odd that it speaks about how Darklings are before they even get taken. Since Seemings are about how you escaped and not how you were before you were taken, it made me a little confused.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/287-wildfire","name":"Wildfire","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-01T02:11:22-07:00","id":498509,"title":"","content":"Couple thoughts. <br /> <br /> I actually really like their backstory, because Seemings, as someone else said, seem to represent now just getting free of Arcadia, but a fundamental need to mature. Painfully. And essentially, having to admit that something held you back, or you were wrong about something, in a prior life. It makes me extremely curious how you'll go from here, because already, the Seemings manage to be improvements on things I thought it was impossible to get better than. And of course, I'm ever curious how you will handle Elementals.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> As for variety, well, there's a lot of things that trust can take. For an example I thought of reading it, imagine someone who was a zealot having their faith in God broken by their Durance. And, when they return, what would they be like? Other examples include Patriotism, any sort of ideological fanatic, and of course, more down to earth things such as family. <br /> <br /> Now, as for the reverse of a Darkling... I don't see them becoming a Darkling because, again, getting a Seeming is clearly, at least in part, about personal growth. You have to be willing to do things you weren't willing to do on Earth, otherwise, you're probably just feeding the very habits that caused you problems to begin with. Someone with no loyalty would become a different Seeming, and have to make a different sort of personal growth. Not necessarily better in morals, but, this isn't about ethics but rather, Maturity. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1657-killer300","name":"Killer300","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"216"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-01T02:59:37-07:00","id":498581,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/498162-second-edition-darklings?p=498257#post498257\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And despite the dislike, I find your take really positive. Thank you. I think I might struggle to play them, too. But I definitely have people in my crew that will love them that way.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, when I said about the dislike, it was not for them, but the type of person they are in the game, I really like what you've done with them, as I hoped to state in my last post... There is quite a bit of potential in telling stories with them... I can see why people in your crew may want to wrangle with playing one of them. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> As an aside, I think if I stat myself with a Seeming, it's looking like Beast so far. Eager to see the remaining four. I was most interested in discovering what makes someone an Elemental, though as mentioned in other places, the Wizened and their transhuman elements beg a look in too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3951-wander","name":"wander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"409"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-01T05:06:18-07:00","id":498659,"title":"","content":"I like this! They give off some genuine pathos, and still manage to be someone I'd want to play. All the things I want to say were taken up by others, so all I can say is great job!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-01T05:39:41-07:00","id":498722,"title":"","content":"Darkling - the anti-hero.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-01T06:03:50-07:00","id":498746,"title":"","content":"The Darkling hit me hard, I didn't expect that, I started crying. Weird reaction, it must of hit a nerve I wasn't aware I had. <br /> <br /> Maybe I there are elements of the Darkling that reseasnate with me on a deep level. I really really like it.<br /> <br /> I don't think the Darkling has to be a jerk all the time or a workaholic, its just that the Darkling does what has to be done, the Hard choices, the Darkling betrays when its needed, not for the heck of it.<br /> <br /> Also the Darkling is the one who is most likely to befriend the lonely, the abadoned people, old folks in retirement home whose kids, if they even have any, don't visit, the lonely virgin in a stripclub's dark corner, the disable person who doesn't get out much, orphans, and the homeless, even the office worker who works so hard, yet who is so often over looked and ignored.<br /> <br /> As for people who start out treacherous to begin with, I have a feeling people like that are more likely to end up Fairiest, Beasts, or Orgers. To Sacrifice the light, your heart, you have to actually have one, perhaps a good one, the Darkness excepts no less.<br /> <br /> Maybe the woman who only married for money did so in order to help her poor family, and a memeber of that family betrays her, maybe the husband she's divorcing bribes her brother, the one she always looked up to, into.testifying on his behalf.<br /> <br /> I love, love, love, love, love this Darkling Seeming, it just connects with me on deep level, so many levels.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-01T06:18:07-07:00","id":498750,"title":"","content":"Anyone Else thought of Sarah Walker in the Darkling discription?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-01T07:08:57-07:00","id":498800,"title":"","content":"It sounds like, the way it's written, that Darklings would not really dig Motleys, as they're coming across a lot more loner. Can a Motley really exist without trust?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/287-wildfire","name":"Wildfire","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-01T07:15:14-07:00","id":498806,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wildfire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/498162-second-edition-darklings?p=498800#post498800\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It sounds like, the way it's written, that Darklings would not really dig Motleys, as they're coming across a lot more loner. Can a Motley really exist without trust?</div> </div> </div> </div> Yes, they can. Because you don't need to worry about trust, just following the letter of the pledge. That's why we have pledges in the first place- for a level of trust with people who could be willing to stab you in the back. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-01T07:44:03-07:00","id":498825,"title":"","content":"I think blessings should have some distinction. It was rather confusing that the blessings for Beasts and Darklings had the same name but did different things.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-01T07:44:33-07:00","id":498826,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/498162-second-edition-darklings?p=498806#post498806\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Yes, they can. Because you don't need to worry about trust, just following the letter of the pledge. That's why we have pledges in the first place- for a level of trust with people who could be willing to stab you in the back.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, you can relax around Motleymates because you know if they screw you over they will <i>pay for it</i>. You aren't trusting in a person, you're trusting in the Wyrd","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/209-that-other-guy","name":"That Other Guy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-01T08:04:28-07:00","id":498850,"title":"","content":"Breaking a Pledge has consquences enbedded right in the magic of the Pledge, so its not blind trust, the Darkling's magic enforces the Pledge giving the Darkling a sense of control. <br /> <br /> Here are some examples of what I think constitutes blind trust.<br /> <br /> The Motley goes on a mission, following the plan is fine for the Darkling, but when something goes wrong on the Fairest's end and the Darkling has no choice, but to trust on the Fairest to fix the situation on the Fly, its hard on the Darkling's mind.<br /> <br /> The Darkling later marries the Fairest, no magical pledge, and the Fairest goes to work in an enviroment where the is alot of temptation to cheat, if the Darkling doesn't keep an eye on the Fairest to make sure she's not straying, its hard on the Darklings sanity, because it required blind trust.<br /> <br /> The Darkling is sick, and only a hedge fruit called the Zizzlestick, can cure her, but she's too sick to go get it herself and in no position to get a pledge out of the Orger, so she has to trust the Orger to save her.<br /> <br /> I think Darklings are naturally inclined towards Pledges in a way that Beasts are inclined away from them. Pledges usually mean they can punish broken promises so they can trust, without it being blind trust because the Darkling has a measure of control of the situtiation, where as the Beast sees the Pledge as confining. A clever Darkling can use pledges as a weapon as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-01T08:16:13-07:00","id":498892,"title":"","content":"So, now Darklings gain clarity when they Shoot the Dog?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","name":"Raistlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-01T08:16:16-07:00","id":498893,"title":"","content":"Just had a thought that a Changelings Seeming could also manifest in the type icons she leaves in the hedge. A Darkling's icons might be shards of her broken heart, perhaps in a more symbolic manner.<br /> <br /> A Beasts, might be signs of her lost humanity, reminders of rules or expectations she followed once that she has since abanddoned.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-01T08:21:36-07:00","id":498894,"title":"","content":"If the dog is about to rip the throat out of another person, who perhaps loves the dog, and can't bare to put the demon possessed dog down, even with they're life on the line. So the Darkling does it for him, spares him that pain and does the horrorible thing of killing the loving loyal dog who had the misfortune to end up demon possessed or magically compelled.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-01T08:25:29-07:00","id":498898,"title":"","content":"Doing bad things for no reason won't get you a dot of clarity, its doing bad things on behalf of someone else because the Darkling feels it needs to be done.<br /> <br /> Darklings are pyschopaths, they're practical people who have learned to do horrible things for the greater good, or maybe not even the greater good, but simply for self preservation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-01T08:29:06-07:00","id":498902,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/498162-second-edition-darklings?p=498398#post498398\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Moving on to The Escape - same issue. It's too specific. It puts a single event and says it's common to every Darkling's backstory. That event being that someone else abandoned them. I just don't think that should be the case. A Darkling could be someone who decided from day one that they'd do anything, and when the opportunity arose they did something terrible. Or maybe it was the Keeper just one day offered freedom if they betrayed another to changeling who was loyal to their fellow slaves and never doubted that loyalty in return, but the changeling made the snap decision to accept.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> &quot;Tell me how the rest of my slaves are planning to escape, and my more loyal thralls shall let you pass unmolested.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 05-01-2015, 11:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-01T08:34:55-07:00","id":498904,"title":"","content":"Fascinating. I see the seeming of the darkling not as the person turning dark but as the person loosing his innocence and naiveness. The changeling has finally learnt that just because you follow the rules and stay loyal doesn't mean that your are entitled to a happy ending. Being good doesn't protect you from bad things. It's a hard and painful lesson to learn but a necessary one. The changeling raises as wiser more mature person and understands that there is no right or wrong, just choices, consequences and whether you can live with those consequences.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","name":"Firanai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2964_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-01T08:53:20-07:00","id":498936,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Firanai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/498162-second-edition-darklings?p=498904#post498904\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fascinating. I see the seeming of the darkling not as the person turning dark but as the person loosing his innocence and naiveness. The changeling has finally learnt that just because you follow the rules and stay loyal doesn't mean that your are entitled to a happy ending. Being good doesn't protect you from bad things. It's a hard and painful lesson to learn but a necessary one. The changeling raises as wiser more mature person and understands that there is no right or wrong, just choices, consequences and whether you can live with those consequences.</div> </div> </div> </div> Actually, I think it is going dark. There's a difference between losing your innocence, and choosing to harm others. Its not that he's lost his innocence, its that he's made an evil choice in order to win their freedom.<br /> <br /> The write up really emphasizes that the Darkling made a choice, one that's haunting him with guilt, something that others would judge them for. The darkling is all about betrayal - both being betrayed, and being the betrayer. He or she chose to screw someone over in order to escape.<br /> <br /> I think that element of choice, of doing something where you're uncomfortable around others in the light, is what really makes the Darkling click. They know what they're doing is wrong, they just justify it to themselves as &quot;necessary evils.&quot; &quot;You can't make an omelette without breaking eggs.&quot; That's pretty dark.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 05-01-2015, 11:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-01T08:59:24-07:00","id":498941,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Raistlin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/498162-second-edition-darklings?p=498892#post498892\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, now Darklings gain clarity when they Shoot the Dog?</div> </div> </div> </div>Weird. My first thought upon reading that bit was Francis Underwood from House of Cards giving his little intro speech about ... well...<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b><a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Frank_Underwood_(House_of_Cards)\" target=\"_blank\">Frank Underwood</a></b>: <i>[watching a dog that has been hit by a car]</i> There are two kinds of pain. The sort of pain that makes you strong. Or useless pain. The sort of pain that's only suffering. I have no patience for useless things. Moments like this require someone who will act. To do the unpleasant thing. The necessary thing... <i>[puts the dog out of its misery]</i> There, no more pain. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-01T09:13:01-07:00","id":498985,"title":"","content":"Frank Underwood, great choice for an example of a Darkling, the dog is just one example of many. Killing redacted is another.<br /> <br /> Doug is another really good example.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2241,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","user":"Omegaphallic","date":". 05-01-2015, 01:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-01T09:50:43-07:00","id":499030,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/498162-second-edition-darklings?p=498936#post498936\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Actually, I think it is going dark. There's a difference between losing your innocence, and choosing to harm others. Its not that he's lost his innocence, its that he's made an evil choice in order to win their freedom.<br /> <br /> The write up really emphasizes that the Darkling made a choice, one that's haunting him with guilt, something that others would judge them for. The darkling is all about betrayal - both being betrayed, and being the betrayer. He or she chose to screw someone over in order to escape.<br /> <br /> I think that element of choice, of doing something where you're uncomfortable around others in the light, is what really makes the Darkling click. They know what they're doing is wrong, they just justify it to themselves as &quot;necessary evils.&quot; &quot;You can't make an omelette without breaking eggs.&quot; That's pretty dark.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Which of course gives the Darklings an appropriate air of fear and unease. In the 1e, it was like &quot;Yeah, they're shadowy. No big deal.&quot; but in 2e, it's like &quot;Okay, so when are they going to put the knife in my back?&quot; Darklings are more scary in this interpretation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-01T10:05:38-07:00","id":499045,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/498162-second-edition-darklings?p=498936#post498936\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Actually, I think it is going dark. There's a difference between losing your innocence, and choosing to harm others. Its not that he's lost his innocence, its that he's made an evil choice in order to win their freedom.<br /> <br /> The write up really emphasizes that the Darkling made a choice, one that's haunting him with guilt, something that others would judge them for. The darkling is all about betrayal - both being betrayed, and being the betrayer. He or she chose to screw someone over in order to escape.<br /> <br /> I think that element of choice, of doing something where you're uncomfortable around others in the light, is what really makes the Darkling click. They know what they're doing is wrong, they just justify it to themselves as &quot;necessary evils.&quot; &quot;You can't make an omelette without breaking eggs.&quot; That's pretty dark.</div> </div> </div> </div>Different tact: Gregory House would be a Darkling Chirurgeon. He's willing to hurt you to heal you, after all.<br /> <br /> The Blessing would trigger if you break it off with your girlfriend because it's not working and she's not willing to recognize that.<br /> The Blessing would trigger if you tell someone's parents about the car crash they died in on Christmas day.<br /> The Blessing would trigger if you make one of your friends go into rehab for their Meth addiction.<br /> <br /> They do it because they <i>care</i>. They know it will hurt in the short term, but that you'll be better for it in the long term, and will appreciate what they did for you if you look back. <hr /><br /> I for one support tweaking the flavor for the Darkling's escape a little bit; the Blessing makes it feel like the reason they got out was <i>making a hard choice</i>, not betrayal. And that fits the Darkling &quot;vibe&quot; better, in my opinion.<br /> <br /> <b>EDIT:</b> Oh and the Scorpion quote thing up top reminded me: Darkling are Scorpion Clan. Think about it for a bit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-01T10:14:18-07:00","id":499070,"title":"","content":"A Darkling Truefriend would be quite a tragedy indeed, eh?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Cxuog44JenzbN7GaAyRqDO4DXce9VGv6ybaCv9yYsPk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Simulacre: An Alternative Morality Stat for Prometheans</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/9523-the-alchemy-lab-homebrew-athanors\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew Athanors</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/887-metamurpho","name":"Metamurpho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar887_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-01T10:27:36-07:00","id":499090,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Killer300</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/498162-second-edition-darklings?p=498509#post498509\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now, as for the reverse of a Darkling... I don't see them becoming a Darkling because, again, getting a Seeming is clearly, at least in part, about personal growth. You have to be willing to do things you weren't willing to do on Earth, otherwise, you're probably just feeding the very habits that caused you problems to begin with. Someone with no loyalty would become a different Seeming, and have to make a different sort of personal growth. Not necessarily better in morals, but, this isn't about ethics but rather, Maturity.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/498162-second-edition-darklings?p=498746#post498746\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for people who start out treacherous to begin with, I have a feeling people like that are more likely to end up Fairiest, Beasts, or Orgers. To Sacrifice the light, your heart, you have to actually have one, perhaps a good one, the Darkness excepts no less.</div> </div> </div> </div>You have to have a heart, but not a very good one. Personal growth doesn't have to mean a 180 change in direction, sometimes it could be walking forwards.<br /> <br /> The gold digger preyed upon people, but she told herself it was only money. She hid behind lawyers and let them do the dirty work, let the lawyers be the ones who had to see the pain in people's eyes.<br /> <br /> Then in Arcadia she came up with a plan, she found the strongest knight among the slaves, charmed him, but she knew he couldn't beat the dragon guarding the exit. As the knight and dragon fight the knight looks at her and says to shout the magic phrase she never had. Every time she closes her eyes she sees the look he gave her when she ran, abandoning her bait to die.<br /> <br /> <br /> A charachter defining Darkling escape from a charachter who was never loyal to anyone pre-Durance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-01T10:42:29-07:00","id":499112,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Metamurpho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/498162-second-edition-darklings?p=499070#post499070\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A Darkling Truefriend would be quite a tragedy indeed, eh?</div> </div> </div> </div> You magnificent bastard... I salute you!<br /> <br /> Seriously, I may have to try and build that concept right now. It definitely is rocking some cool ideas!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-01T10:48:48-07:00","id":499118,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/498162-second-edition-darklings?p=498985#post498985\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Frank Underwood, great choice for an example of a Darkling, the dog is just one example of many. Killing [<b>REDACTED</b>]is another.</div> </div> </div> </div>May want to edit that for major spoilers","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/209-that-other-guy","name":"That Other Guy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-01T11:01:40-07:00","id":499128,"title":"","content":"Actually given that True Friends are chosen to be companions, and often escaping could entail leaving said companion behind after said companion trusted them, I can see True Friend Darklings as common.<br /> <br /> When inspiring others the True Friend cloaks it liberally in lies, the True Friends doesn't make a steadfast bond lightly, only after the person proves themselves, and ultimately the True Friend goes mad as his darkling nature wars with his TF nature.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-01T11:15:08-07:00","id":499135,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/498162-second-edition-darklings?p=499090#post499090\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> You have to have a heart, but not a very good one. Personal growth doesn't have to mean a 180 change in direction, sometimes it could be walking forwards.<br /> <br /> The gold digger preyed upon people, but she told herself it was only money. She hid behind lawyers and let them do the dirty work, let the lawyers be the ones who had to see the pain in people's eyes.<br /> <br /> Then in Arcadia she came up with a plan, she found the strongest knight among the slaves, charmed him, but she knew he couldn't beat the dragon guarding the exit. As the knight and dragon fight the knight looks at her and says to shout the magic phrase she never had. Every time she closes her eyes she sees the look he gave her when she ran, abandoning her bait to die.<br /> <br /> <br /> A charachter defining Darkling escape from a charachter who was never loyal to anyone pre-Durance.</div> </div> </div> </div> I still say that sounds like what I'm guessing Fairest would be like, a social manipulator who works through others (not that Darklings can lie of course).<br /> <br /> The Loyalty is important to the Darkling concept because something has to be sacrificed, in the Darklings case it loyalty, that's the light that gets put out.<br /> <br /> This doesn't mean that the Darkling's couldn't be a bastard before hand, cruel even, just that they were loyal to something or someone. A Darkling knows what they did is wrong, they may rationalize the why, but not its nature.<br /> <br /> So that lady in your example, maybe she has a son who turns her in, maybe she started out a devoted wife, but was betrayed so she descides to betrayal future husbands. Maybe she saw the father she adored kill her mother and decides no one will ever do that to her, so she divorces men who love her for money.<br /> <br /> Its this that makes Darklings compelling and relatable, they're not simply jerks for shits and giggles or greed, betrayal isn't an ends to a means, it has meaning for them.<br /> <br /> Just like confinement has great meaning for beasts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-01T11:25:10-07:00","id":499143,"title":"","content":"Damn. I wasn't a huge fan of Darklings in 1e, but this? This I love. This makes me want to play a Darkling. Unless the writeup for Wizend (my favorite Seeming in 1e) hits home for me like this one did, I may have a new favorite.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-01T11:30:38-07:00","id":499158,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/498162-second-edition-darklings?p=499135#post499135\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Loyalty is important to the Darkling concept because something has to be sacrificed, in the Darklings case it loyalty, that's the light that gets put out.</div> </div> </div> </div>You know, I don't actually think that's true.<br /> <br /> Rereading The Escape, the word loyal doesn't appear even once.<br /> <br /> A libarian looking after their Keeper's enormous archive of dangerous books who discovers an invisibility spell that requires killing another Changeling; and uses that spell to escape. That fits the write up for a Darkling's Escape - and it's something I could see my golddigger example doing.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-01T11:44:45-07:00","id":499184,"title":"","content":"Together with the stuff on Beasts, I'm seeing a really interesting trend for 2nd Edition. Beasts are people who always felt trapped by rules and decide to break them all. Darklings are people who had always been too trusting, and are forced to accept that they can't trust anyone. With these in mind, here are my guesses for the themes of the other seemings:<br /> <br /> Elementals: People who had always been flashy and attention seeking. They escape by learning to fade into the background. Sort of like the opposite of Beasts.<br /> Fairest: People who had always been untrusting and anti social. They escape by learning to work with other people. Sort of the opposite of Darklings.<br /> Ogres: People who had always felt inadequate and unworthy. They escape by learning that they have the power to do what they want. Sort of opposite of Wizened.<br /> Wizened: People who had always felt that they were perfect with no room to grow. They escape by learning that they still have improving to do. Sort of the opposite of Ogres.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2283-andreamus","name":"andreamus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2283_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-01T11:46:47-07:00","id":499185,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/498162-second-edition-darklings?p=498936#post498936\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Actually, I think it is going dark. There's a difference between losing your innocence, and choosing to harm others. Its not that he's lost his innocence, its that he's made an evil choice in order to win their freedom.<br /> <br /> The write up really emphasizes that the Darkling made a choice, one that's haunting him with guilt, something that others would judge them for. The darkling is all about betrayal - both being betrayed, and being the betrayer. He or she chose to screw someone over in order to escape.<br /> <br /> I think that element of choice, of doing something where you're uncomfortable around others in the light, is what really makes the Darkling click. They know what they're doing is wrong, they just justify it to themselves as &amp;quot;necessary evils.&amp;quot; &amp;quot;You can't make an omelette without breaking eggs.&amp;quot; That's pretty dark.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's a fine line between pragmatism and treachery, and Darklings certainly seem to walk that line, by the looks of this writeup. I would say the change is absolutely about loss of na\u00efvet\u00e9. But since that loss is brought on by abuse, trauma, and abandonment, the Darkling has a tendency to overcorrect. Placing complete trust in another is a Clarity Breaking Point because simply being in a situation that could lead to bring betrayed or abandoned again is triggering. They're so afraid of being hurt again that they fear to even be in a position where such a betrayal is possible. They regain clarity when they make the &quot;tough choices&quot; because it reaffirms the idea that it was shedding their innocence that saved them. It reassures them that what they did was <i>right</i>. That they <i>had to do</i> what they did, and it's <i>everyone else</i> that's being held back by foolish notions of loyalty and fair play.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-01T11:51:01-07:00","id":499189,"title":"","content":"Your right, the escape doesn't meantion loyalty, but background does majorly, the Darkling doesn't have to be loyal to someone in Arcadia in order to screw them other. Heck even in the bsckground it says many, so they're be exceptions.<br /> <br /> Still, I think the loyalty angle in the background makes the would be character more interesting, more compelling. Adds some relatablity, extra drama, the way that the beasts have feeling confined by human rules and expectations gives them more depth.<br /> <br /> Still each to thier own.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-01T12:00:56-07:00","id":499205,"title":"","content":"Arguing that loyalty is interesting is not the same as arguing that the Seeming write up should be written in such a way to imply loyalty is the only option.<br /> <br /> I agree that loyalty is interesting, I just don't see why it should be so much more promiment than other possibilities.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-01T12:02:55-07:00","id":499208,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/498162-second-edition-darklings?p=499135#post499135\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I still say that sounds like what I'm guessing Fairest would be like, a social manipulator who works through others (not that Darklings can lie of course).<br /> <br /> The Loyalty is important to the Darkling concept because something has to be sacrificed, in the Darklings case it loyalty, that's the light that gets put out.<br /> <br /> This doesn't mean that the Darkling's couldn't be a bastard before hand, cruel even, just that they were loyal to something or someone. A Darkling knows what they did is wrong, they may rationalize the why, but not its nature.<br /> <br /> So that lady in your example, maybe she has a son who turns her in, maybe she started out a devoted wife, but was betrayed so she descides to betrayal future husbands. Maybe she saw the father she adored kill her mother and decides no one will ever do that to her, so she divorces men who love her for money.<br /> <br /> Its this that makes Darklings compelling and relatable, they're not simply jerks for shits and giggles or greed, betrayal isn't an ends to a means, it has meaning for them.<br /> <br /> Just like confinement has great meaning for beasts.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <br /> You're right. If there's nothing to sacrifice then the Changeling would have turned into their Seeming the moment they stepped through the Hedge. You can't sacrifice loyalty if you never had any to begin with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-01T12:02:56-07:00","id":499209,"title":"","content":"For Fairest I'd say self reliant instead of antisocial, they might like people, people might like them, but they lived in a way that they didn't need help or others, until one day something happens, they need help, or someones cooperation, and they talk someone into doing what they want. They then find a keeper who offers help as well, perhaps with an unexpected price. To escape they learn to rely on others, perhaps even to lead others, but at a price, they sacrifice they're self reliance, they need people now, even if only for company. A Blessing when manipulating someone into helping you or doing something they wouldn't ordinarily do gets one clarity. Curse, the Fairest loses clarity when she isolates herself, refusing help, or to rely on anyone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-01T12:04:23-07:00","id":499212,"title":"","content":"What other possiblities did you have in mind Raven?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-01T12:05:18-07:00","id":499213,"title":"","content":"They provide a very wide idea of what constitutes loyalty.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-01T12:09:30-07:00","id":499220,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/498162-second-edition-darklings?p=499212#post499212\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What other possiblities did you have in mind Raven?</div> </div> </div> </div>I would say that every possible charachter is a possibility for a Darkling.<br /> <br /> If you escaped by screwing someone over, you're a Darkling. Anyone can choose to screw someone over, so anyone can be a Darkling.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-01T12:14:04-07:00","id":499243,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/498162-second-edition-darklings?p=499205#post499205\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Arguing that loyalty is interesting is not the same as arguing that the Seeming write up should be written in such a way to imply loyalty is the only option.<br /> <br /> I agree that loyalty is interesting, I just don't see why it should be so much more promiment than other possibilities.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think it is. There's a lot of &quot;often&quot;s and &quot;tend to&quot;s in there. I think the pre-durance descriptions are there to give an idea of what kind of person is likely to end up making their escape by the means that will make them into the corresponding Seeming. People who were loyal and trusting in their human lives are likely to be taken advantage of in Arcadia, and therefore have to turn themselves into untrusting pragmatists in order to end that cycle of abuse. People who lived their human lives in cages (figuratively speaking) are likely to be improsoned in Arcadia, and therefore have to turn themselves into wild animals in order to free themselves from that bondage. That doesn't mean other people can't fall victim to those abuses, or use those means to reclaim agency, but the writeups give an idea of what kinds of narratives generally lead a person to become that Seeming. If you've got another concept that fits, there's nothing stopping you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 05-01-2015, 03:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-01T12:36:45-07:00","id":499258,"title":"","content":"They do say many, not all, so you can build Darklings or Beasts that don't fit the background, its just most do fit it. The True Fae have prefered types, but they might not always stick with that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-01T12:56:14-07:00","id":499271,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/498162-second-edition-darklings?p=499205#post499205\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Arguing that loyalty is interesting is not the same as arguing that the Seeming write up should be written in such a way to imply loyalty is the only option.<br /> <br /> I agree that loyalty is interesting, I just don't see why it should be so much more promiment than other possibilities.</div> </div> </div> </div>Because I'd argue the background matters a lot more for the Seeming. To counter your earlier example, she isn't really sacrificing anything, she's only expanding a toolset she already has. <br /> <br /> So far, the whole point of becoming a Seeming is to admit that your prior way of doing things didn't work, and that you're going to have to make sacrifices from a fundamental values perspective to move forwards with your life. The Beast is giving up society's rules so as to escape, and all the comforts that implies. Same, a Darkling giving up loyalty as a concept means having to accept that their prior value structure was fundamentally flawed. <br /> <br /> This, by the way, would give another reason, among many, why there aren't many Changelings. Giving up part of your own value structure is probably one of the hardest types of personal change imaginable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1657-killer300","name":"Killer300","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"216"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-01T12:58:05-07:00","id":499274,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/498162-second-edition-darklings?p=499220#post499220\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would say that every possible charachter is a possibility for a Darkling.<br /> <br /> If you escaped by screwing someone over, you're a Darkling. Anyone can choose to screw someone over, so anyone can be a Darkling.</div> </div> </div> </div>But what about Fairest? I think we're going to have the see the rest of the Seemings before we figure out how much... breadth, if you will, the Seemings have. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1657-killer300","name":"Killer300","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"216"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-01T13:08:21-07:00","id":499283,"title":"","content":"Also, to give some more thoughts to Fairest, <br /> <br /> I think its going to be a case of giving up... well, independence. An opposite, if you will, to Beasts. You're someone who wasn't dependent on people and society, or otherwise ignored them. Becoming a Fairest was that you utilized other persons to escape in a much more explicit way, and in the process, had to admit you fundamentally needed other people. <br /> <br /> Now, another part of this however is also learning how to not just Manipulate, but again Trust. They'd also be an opposite to Darklings, because they would need to gain the trust of other persons.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1657-killer300","name":"Killer300","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"216"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-01T13:21:13-07:00","id":499307,"title":"","content":"So looks like its safe to say that Seemings are the scars from what you did versus Kiths as the scars from what was done to you. Like with Beasts, I'm definitely seeing a lot here that can be mined for ideas. I also just want to say I'm honestly really impressed that the metaphor shift is going as cleanly as it is. It makes me optimistic for the stuff we haven't seen yet.<br /> <br /> If you're going in the standard order for Seemings, I'm guessing Elementals will be the next ones up. I'm really interested to see how they work considering they're far and away the most high concept of the Seemings. I know they were hands down the most discussed in the prior brainspew thread, so it will be interesting to see where you've gone with them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3738-illuminated-minutia","name":"Illuminated Minutia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3738_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-01T13:54:38-07:00","id":499363,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/498162-second-edition-darklings?p=499243#post499243\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think it is. There's a lot of &quot;often&quot;s and &quot;tend to&quot;s in there.</div> </div> </div> </div> Has it been edited? Either my memory is playing tricks on me or those weren't there this morning, in which case it's a step in the right direction <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/498162-second-edition-darklings?p=499243#post499243\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I think the pre-durance descriptions are there to give an idea of what kind of person is likely to end up making their escape by the means that will make them into the corresponding Seeming.</div> </div> </div> </div> That would work better if it gave several examples rather than just one. For example, you say &quot;loyal and trusting&quot; but the write up doesn't saying trusting; just loyal and in fact it gives an example of someone who isn't trusting but is loyal anyway - the housewife who knows she's being cheated on.<br /> <br /> Having loyal and trusting as two different traits which could lead to a Darkling like durance would be better than just one. &quot;backstabing&quot; as a third trait, would be better than just two.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Killer300</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/498162-second-edition-darklings?p=499271#post499271\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because I'd argue the background matters a lot more for the Seeming. To counter your earlier example, she isn't really sacrificing anything, she's only expanding a toolset she already has.</div> </div> </div> </div> By pushing her dark methods beyond the limits she created to justify them to herself she's sacrificing her sense of self-respect.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Killer300</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/498162-second-edition-darklings?p=499271#post499271\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So far, the whole point of becoming a Seeming is to admit that your prior way of doing things didn't work</div> </div> </div> </div> We've already been explicitly told that the whole point of a Seeming is how you took back control.<br /> <br /> If you say that the only possible way to take back control is to go against your previous philosohpy of life then you <u>didn't taken back control</u>. You played to the Keeper's script - the Keeper decided that it would be fun to see if this loyal person can be turned into a backstabber, and they did.<br /> <br /> The whole concept of a Seeming being the way you took back your own destiny only works if each changeling had the chance to become several different Seemings; if they don't have a choice then by definition they aren't taking back their destiny.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Killer300</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/498162-second-edition-darklings?p=499274#post499274\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But what about Fairest? I think we're going to have the see the rest of the Seemings before we figure out how much... breadth, if you will, the Seemings have.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm sure we'll find out soon enough. Though at a guess.<br /> <br /> A Darkling escaped by doing something immoral.<br /> A Fairest escaped by manipulating someone. It doesn't have to actually be immoral.<br /> <br /> There are probably lots of edge cases that could be either. After all, betraying a friend is a huge social no-no so in theory that could make a Beast.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-01T14:14:20-07:00","id":499379,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/498162-second-edition-darklings?p=499363#post499363\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Has it been edited? Either my memory is playing tricks on me or those weren't there this morning, in which case it's a step in the right direction <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> That would work better if it gave several examples rather than just one. For example, you say &quot;loyal and trusting&quot; but the write up doesn't saying trusting; just loyal and in fact it gives an example of someone who isn't trusting but is loyal anyway - the housewife who knows she's being cheated on.<br /> <br /> Having loyal and trusting as two different traits which could lead to a Darkling like durance would be better than just one. &quot;backstabing&quot; as a third trait, would be better than just two.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, the other example was an old company man, so there's that.<br /> <br /> Note, I'm only arguing, in hindsight, why this would be the most common background, you're right it shouldn't be the only, although I don't think your counter-example is the best.<br /> <br /> For a different one, I could see, for example, see a... umm, relatively normal person who doesn't strong values in either direction in regards to loyalty becoming a Darkling, I just don't see someone who already embraces being a betrayer becoming a Darkling. Its emphasizing a part of their personality they already possessed and doesn't really let them have any personal growth, because they get to rely on something they were already good at.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> By pushing her dark methods beyond the limits she created to justify them to herself she's sacrificing her sense of self-respect.<br /> <br /> We've already been explicitly told that the whole point of a Seeming is how you took back control.<br /> <br /> If you say that the only possible way to take back control is to go against your previous philosohpy of life then you <u>didn't taken back control</u>. You played to the Keeper's script - the Keeper decided that it would be fun to see if this loyal person can be turned into a backstabber, and they did. </div> </div> </div>Not really. For one, you're doing something that is against your prior personality and value structure. Why would the Keeper expect that? Additionally, you did gain Agency from doing so, because in each case, your prior value structure, personality, and similar were what was holding you down as a person. Loyalty and Trust in this case put limits on you, in the case of the Beast, it was being in a Cage, whether literal or metaphorical, before hand. You're not just breaking free of the Keeper, but of your own personal limitations.<br /> <br /> Just because you gain Agency doesn't mean you didn't have to sacrifice something for it, which I think is the key here.<br /> <br /> We're not even touching on that acting as you previously, just more so, would also be something the Keeper expects. Your prior example wouldn't work under that the Keeper expects someone who was already a backstabber in life to do so later on. They probably wouldn't let them be in a position where they can exploit that, by say making them something that cannot speak at all, say a statue(as does occur), or isolating them from other Changelings to the point they, again, have no means of using that skill set.<br /> <br /> Obviously, the above has flaws, however, if we're getting into what the Keeper expects, that cuts both ways.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The whole concept of a Seeming being the way you took back your own destiny only works if each changeling had the chance to become several different Seemings; if they don't have a choice then by definition they aren't taking back their destiny. </div> </div> </div>Sure, but, we have several separate value structures. There's a lot of different ways the same character could become a Seeming. To take the loyal housewife, she could interpret her prior life as a gilded cage, and become the Beast to break free of both learned behaviors along with Arcadia.<br /> <br /> I'd argue for Seemings to work, there also has to be many reasons why everyone who gets taken to Arcadia can't pull it off, and I'd argue part of it should be that it requires painful personal growth to pull off.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1657-killer300","name":"Killer300","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"216"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-01T14:32:02-07:00","id":499395,"title":"","content":"Seemings are about &quot;doing what must be done.&quot; They're the survival part of the survivor metaphor. They <i>will</i> change you. You had to abandon your humanity. You had to betray someone's trust. You had to let go of your Self. You had to accept you weren't strong enough as you were and jam an arc reactor in your chest. Those things stay with you. The external trappings are just Faerie making your outside reflect your inside. You made it through an experience so utterly horrible that the only way to survive was to let go of something. When the smoke clears you can't just go and pick it back up. It's gone and you'll probably never get it back.<br /> <br /> Although, if letting go of your trust in others let you survive <i>Faerie</i> did you ever really need it to begin with? Maybe you <i>are</i> better off.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3738-illuminated-minutia","name":"Illuminated Minutia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3738_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-01T14:35:42-07:00","id":499402,"title":"","content":"&quot;This, by the way, would give another reason, among many, why there aren't many Changelings. Giving up part of your own value structure is probably one of the hardest types of personal change imaginable.&quot;<br /> <br /> Damn right it is, its like cutting out a chuck of your soul.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-01T14:47:23-07:00","id":499413,"title":"","content":"I think Elemental will be the opposite of beasts, instead of rejecting they're humanity in favoure of they're beastly side, they reject the beastly animal side, in favour of they're logic unemotional side.<br /> <br /> Or it could be about purging themselves of impurities, they're imperfections.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-01T17:16:44-07:00","id":499512,"title":"","content":"&quot;Don't ask me what I did. Because if you ask, I'll tell you.&quot; <br /> <br /> -Eliot Spencer, Leverage","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-01T17:39:47-07:00","id":499550,"title":"","content":"By the way, I just thought of something.<br /> <br /> If your Seeming is the result of you escaping, then how will Loyalists be portrayed in 2e? If they're still working for the Keeper, then shouldn't they not possess a Seeming?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-01T17:46:50-07:00","id":499552,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/498162-second-edition-darklings?p=499550#post499550\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">By the way, I just thought of something.<br /> <br /> If your Seeming is the result of you escaping, then how will Loyalists be portrayed in 2e? If they're still working for the Keeper, then shouldn't they not possess a Seeming?</div> </div> </div> </div>Again, the Seeming isn't so much how you escaped as how you regained your Agency. It's just that with your average PC, those two things are often related. With Loyalists, it would be decided by how you came to decide to serve the Gentry rather than fight them. Maybe they turned in a fellow changeling whose escape put the rest of their group at risk, becoming a Darkling.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2283-andreamus","name":"andreamus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2283_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-01T17:57:49-07:00","id":499563,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>andreamus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/498162-second-edition-darklings?p=499552#post499552\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Again, the Seeming isn't so much how you escaped as how you regained your Agency. It's just that with your average PC, those two things are often related. With Loyalists, it would be decided by how you came to decide to serve the Gentry rather than fight them. Maybe they turned in a fellow changeling whose escape put the rest of their group at risk, becoming a Darkling.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I suppose that makes sense as a possibility. ^_^","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-01T18:05:18-07:00","id":499569,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>andreamus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/498162-second-edition-darklings?p=499184#post499184\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ogres: People who had always felt inadequate and unworthy. They escape by learning that they have the power to do what they want. Sort of opposite of Wizened.</div> </div> </div> </div>I believe it was mentioned that Ogres are going to be about Consumption.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/287-wildfire","name":"Wildfire","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-01T18:05:19-07:00","id":499570,"title":"","content":"I'm pretty sure Dave H. said Loyalists will have no Seeming.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-01T18:10:51-07:00","id":499573,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/498162-second-edition-darklings?p=499570#post499570\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm pretty sure Dave H. said Loyalists will have no Seeming.</div> </div> </div> </div>Most of the time. I mean, there will be edge cases. But, most Loyalists will not have one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-01T18:20:27-07:00","id":499582,"title":"","content":"I really like the themes touched on here. Doing what what has to be done and choosing pragmatism over morality / value has a lot of narrative space to explore. I really like how Seemings sort of imply the type of stories that the characters are &quot;meant&quot; to tell without actually constraining them to that mold. Nothing annoys me more than picking up a game and going, &quot;okay, but what are the PCs supposed to <i>do</i>?&quot; The writing direction is pretty evocative, if rough (joys of first draft).<br /> <br /> I'd like to echo The King's Raven's point on Page 2 about it being too specific, and expand on that point by saying it's largely a matter of presentation and formatting. I think a format similar to Blood and Smoke's presentation of Clans may be exceptionally appropriate and helpful here. Start off with a quote to set the mood. Distill the essence of the Seeming into about three paragraphs. Then give several examples that demonstrate a mortal archetype getting taken to Arcadia, taking agency (in a way that's appropriate to the Seeming) and escaping. That gives a firm foundational stereotype to build off of and helps new players unfamiliar with Changeling to get a better idea of what getting to Arcadia and escaping <i>looks</i> like. However, since they'd still be examples, it would allow you the best of both worlds since examples only imply the norm instead of mandate it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-01T18:48:01-07:00","id":499631,"title":"","content":"Oh hey, tangentially important for contextualizing these escapes / agency. Do Changelings still come back from Arcadia because of a cherished memory of home? How does that work with Seemings?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-01T21:38:59-07:00","id":499780,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/498162-second-edition-darklings?p=499512#post499512\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Don't ask me what I did. Because if you ask, I'll tell you.&quot;<br /> <br /> -Eliot Spencer, Leverage</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ayP14Mk_Q9A&amp;t=10m\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ayP14Mk_Q9A&amp;t=10m\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ayP14Mk_Q9A&amp;t=10m\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ayP14Mk_Q9A&amp;t=10m </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> &quot;The two of us, we do things they can't. Won't.&quot;<br /> &quot;Does that make us bad?&quot;<br /> &quot;It makes us ..Us. Now, you can take that as a gift or you can take it as a curse, but that's up to you.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":226,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","user":"BrilliantRain","date":". 05-02-2015, 12:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-01T21:51:17-07:00","id":499785,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/498162-second-edition-darklings?p=499780#post499780\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ayP14Mk_Q9A&amp;t=10m\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ayP14Mk_Q9A&amp;t=10m\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ayP14Mk_Q9A&amp;t=10m\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ayP14Mk_Q9A&amp;t=10m </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> &quot;The two of us, we do things they can't. Won't.&quot;<br /> &quot;Does that make us bad?&quot;<br /> &quot;It makes us ..Us. Now, you can take that as a gift or you can take it as a curse, but that's up to you.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> It's like Erwin's plan to capture the Titan. <br /> <br /> Well playing this by the books is just racking up a death toll. Time to try something desperate. I'm going to need live bait!<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-01T21:55:49-07:00","id":499786,"title":"","content":"&quot;Sometimes you have to break a thing to fix it. No one wants to be the one to do that. But someone has to, and that person has to be comfortable with being thought of as the jerk, the asshole, the dick. Someone has to be the bad guy if this is going to change. And no one-<i>no one</i>-is as comfortable being the bad guy as I am.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-01T22:49:56-07:00","id":499844,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/498162-second-edition-darklings?p=499780#post499780\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ayP14Mk_Q9A&amp;t=10m\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ayP14Mk_Q9A&amp;t=10m\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ayP14Mk_Q9A&amp;t=10m\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ayP14Mk_Q9A&amp;t=10m </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> &quot;The two of us, we do things they can't. Won't.&quot;<br /> &quot;Does that make us bad?&quot;<br /> &quot;It makes us ..Us. Now, you can take that as a gift or you can take it as a curse, but that's up to you.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I just watched that episode again last night. It tears me up every time. Ironically, I absolutely cannot relate to the client at all. I think rich people doing dangerous things deserve all the stupid things that happen to them. <br /> <br /> But Eliot and Parker's bit there... That's fucking powerful. <br /> <br /> Also? The joke about the spetznaz guys and their distinctive footprints is a line from one of my pieces in the Leverage RPG. So it tickles me every time I hear it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-01T23:15:13-07:00","id":499883,"title":"","content":"So as anyone knows it's easy to criticise and hard to pick up the pen and do better; so hard in fact that I had to sleep on it to come up with something I like - but now I have <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Here's how I would rework the Background to capture what I consider that key idea that anyone could become any Seeming - it's not who they were, it's the choice they made.<br /> <br /> MachineIV I'd really appreciate your feedback, even if you don't use it I'd like to hear what you think works and what you think doesn't.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Background:</b> Once upon a time there was a loyal company man, but the other slaves didn't return his loyalty but in Arcadia his loyalty to his fellow slaves made him a target. When he realised this he betrayed them and won his freedom. She was a gold digger, devoicing a string of men for their money. When she seduced someone to sacrifice them for her freedom she realised just how far she'd go. He was a priest, and after every day of backbreaking labour he would comfort the other slaves with tales of Jesus. Then he saw the book of spells and saw his path to freedom, but suffer not the witch to live.<br /> <br /> What makes me a good person? Is it loyalty, piety, compassion or something else? Given time to think most people, even gangsters and serial killers, can rattle off dozens of traits that in their own eyes make them a good person. Becoming a Darkling doesn't take dozens, it only takes one trait.<br /> <br /> <b>The Escape: S</b>he did what she had to do to escape. In her mind, or in reality, that meant screwing someone else over. It meant leaving someone behind. It meant taking advantage of the situation and making the hard choice not the right choice. She remembered what makes her a good person, and turned her back on it. And in that decision, she let shadows in, she accepted it in and abandoned the light and righteous path. She decided, in that key moment, that the righteous are fools or liars, and she would be neither. But it broke her heart into a thousand shards, glinting in the shadows around her.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 05-03-2015, 03:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-01T23:23:15-07:00","id":499890,"title":"","content":"Reading this does make me wonder if a Changeling can ever get that part of themselves back? I mean, yes, you can't go back to who you were and everything, but, say I wanted to tell a story of a Darkling learning to be able to open up and trust again, even just a little bit. Their Seeming Curse kinda cuts that story off at the knees, so, is there a way to get rid of the Curse? Or something else that could enable those kinds of stories?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-01T23:40:30-07:00","id":499903,"title":"","content":"I'm wondering where my current 1e Changeling will end up if I update him.<br /> <br /> I've not concentrated so much on his Seeming and kith, but he's a changeling gifted in Oneiromancy where often times others don't want him anywhere their dreamscape, because of a multitude of reasons. His story is he tries to find a way to tout it, eventually turning to becoming a salesman in the Goblin Market. I've not given much thought to long-term aspirations, though thats his primary plot arc going into a game at least. The old good ones of defeating the Keeper make a fair long term aspiration, though I secretly want his story to end by him being so low Clarity and High Wyrd he actually <i>replaces</i> his Keeper in Arcadia... His story in a way is to trying to find a connection with another, to hold Dream Pledges long-term with someone and I think his Seeming will really flavour just how that story tells itself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3951-wander","name":"wander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"409"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-01T23:46:37-07:00","id":499912,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/498162-second-edition-darklings?p=499890#post499890\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Reading this does make me wonder if a Changeling can ever get that part of themselves back? I mean, yes, you can't go back to who you were and everything, but, say I wanted to tell a story of a Darkling learning to be able to open up and trust again, even just a little bit. Their Seeming Curse kinda cuts that story off at the knees, so, is there a way to get rid of the Curse? Or something else that could enable those kinds of stories?</div> </div> </div> </div>One possible solution is to say that trusting other's isn't a Breaking Point, but if your trust was misplaced the consiquences are significantly magnified. Maybe every Clarity breaking point involving misplaced trust is magnified by one level. Exceptional Success becomes Success. Success becomes Failure. Failure becomes Dramatic Failure. Dramatic Failure is still a Dramatic Failure.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 05-02-2015, 05:19 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-01T23:59:44-07:00","id":499926,"title":"","content":"The curse concerns me, given as it is in the draft. There have never needed to be more reasons for changelings <i>not </i>to trust others. If anything, in Lost 1st edition it could already be difficult enough for motleys to form and function well. I can see the curse making interactions needlessly difficult and tedious for an unknown length of time within the group and/or keeping characters distant even when they should otherwise be warming up to each other. Relying on pledges for everything with everyone forever to have any kind of trust seems a bit much to ask of the player and the group. Some serious reconsideration and rewriting will help.<br /> <br /> Less focus on the former loyal pushover angle and more of an opening up to various types of Darkling backgrounds would be nice, as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kismet's <a href=\"http://www.wod.kismetrose.com/\" target=\"_blank\">WOD</a> - <a href=\"http://www.dnd.kismetrose.com/\" target=\"_blank\">D&amp;D</a> - <a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/BoundinDreams\" target=\"_blank\">C:tL</a> - <a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/TheNamelessEmpire\" target=\"_blank\">M:tC</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/227-kismetrose","name":"KismetRose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar227_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-02T03:17:59-07:00","id":500080,"title":"","content":"I agree in part with KingsRaven. The write up is very specific, (altough well-written and very evocative) This feels at odds with how wide-ranging Changeling generally is regarding characters. I think these elements should be re-worded to be more broad.<br /> <br /> The Background. The focus on Loyalty making some-one a push over seems forced to me. People who stubbornly adhere to one set of behavior leads to inflexibility but are not inherently push-overs.<br /> <br /> I went back and looked over the 1st Edition Darkling write up. That one focuses more on Darklings learning to adapt to survive their durances. I personally prefer this theme. If the background section could focus more on Darklings being set in their ways, and then their escape forcing them to ADAPT or SACRIFICE rather than BETRAY this would make me a lot happier. The theme of comprimise and sacrifice and making hard choices and is still there, but its then up to the player to decide whether that meant actually leaving someone behind or whether it was a personality aspect that was lost (happiness, trust.)<br /> <br /> A wispy, not quite there, character that is easy to forget because they left behind their former charm. A perpetual Wallflower, Spring courtier.<br /> <br /> A weak, wimpy character who left behind she chronic selflessness to become a strong warrior. Summer courtier type.<br /> <br /> I think the focus moving from the escape involving betrayal to adapting would make this archtype more broad and spark more concepts for more players.<br /> <br /> Finally, as an aside, I would love it if the character concepts for all seemings were written in a more fairy tale esqe fashion.<br /> <br /> Eg, She's the Thief that moves in the shadows. No one sees her as she skips through their gaze, robbing them blind, sometimes literally. The twist? She never steals from rightful owners.<br /> <br /> (Not the best example, off the top of my head but a more fairy tale tone as an example.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1161,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1161-gravitas-man","user":"Gravitas Man","date":". 05-02-2015, 09:18 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1161-gravitas-man","name":"Gravitas Man","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1161_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-02T04:39:19-07:00","id":500140,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/498162-second-edition-darklings?p=499912#post499912\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> One possible solution is to say that trusting other's isn't a Breaking Point, but if your trust was misplaced the consiquences are significantly magnified. Maybe every Clarity breaking point involving misplaced trust is magnified by one level. Exceptional Success becomes Success. Success becomes Failure. Failure becomes Dramatic Failure. Dramatic Failure is still a Dramatic Failure.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <br /> Guys, it's okay for a Darkling to trust somebody, it's just not okay for them to put <b>blind trust</b> in somebody. Not having a plan B, an escape route prepared, or properly surveying the area beforehand.<br /> <br /> A Darkling doesn't say &quot;I'm doing this my way.&quot; when presented with a plan by somebody. They say &quot;It sounds decent enough, but here's another option if it fails.&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> If a Darkling was incapable of trusting anybody, they might as well be a single player game.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> OH, by the way; has anybody noticed that Darklings don't seem weakened by exposure to sunlight anymore?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 05-02-2015, 07:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-02T07:12:19-07:00","id":500291,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gravitas Man</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/498162-second-edition-darklings?p=500080#post500080\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I agree in part with KingsRaven. The write up is very specific, (altough well-written and very evocative) This feels at odds with how wide-ranging Changeling generally is regarding characters. I think these elements should be re-worded to be more broad.<br /> <br /> The Background. The focus on Loyalty making some-one a push over seems forced to me. People who stubbornly adhere to one set of behavior leads to inflexibility but are not inherently push-overs.<br /> <br /> I went back and looked over the 1st Edition Darkling write up. That one focuses more on Darklings learning to adapt to survive their durances. I personally prefer this theme. If the background section could focus more on Darklings being set in their ways, and then their escape forcing them to ADAPT or SACRIFICE rather than BETRAY this would make me a lot happier. The theme of comprimise and sacrifice and making hard choices and is still there, but its then up to the player to decide whether that meant actually leaving someone behind or whether it was a personality aspect that was lost (happiness, trust.)<br /> <br /> A wispy, not quite there, character that is easy to forget because they left behind their former charm. A perpetual Wallflower, Spring courtier.<br /> <br /> A weak, wimpy character who left behind she chronic selflessness to become a strong warrior. Summer courtier type.<br /> <br /> I think the focus moving from the escape involving betrayal to adapting would make this archtype more broad and spark more concepts for more players.<br /> <br /> Finally, as an aside, I would love it if the character concepts for all seemings were written in a more fairy tale esqe fashion.<br /> <br /> Eg, She's the Thief that moves in the shadows. No one sees her as she skips through their gaze, robbing them blind, sometimes literally. The twist? She never steals from rightful owners.<br /> <br /> (Not the best example, off the top of my head but a more fairy tale tone as an example.)</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm sorry, but I just totally disagree here. The Darklings never made much sense to me in 1e. The whole adaptable thing was not terribly interesting, and didn't follow through very well to why that made them creatures of darkness. If the new take on Kith and Seeming is that Kith is how your Keeper changed you and Seeming is how you changed yourself, than Darklings need to have made themselves darker to escape. Adaptability is just not dark, it's a pretty universally positive quality. Maybe the writeup focuses too much on loyalty and betrayal? I don't think so, but enough people seem to find it too narrow, so I guess that could be a way to improve. But I think it's important not to lose the fact that for someone to change themselves into a creature of the darkness in order to escape their Durance, they need to have had a light within them to begin with, and they need to have made the choice to let that light go out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-02T07:16:30-07:00","id":500296,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/498162-second-edition-darklings?p=499209#post499209\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For Fairest I'd say self reliant instead of antisocial, they might like people, people might like them, but they lived in a way that they didn't need help or others, until one day something happens, they need help, or someones cooperation, and they talk someone into doing what they want. They then find a keeper who offers help as well, perhaps with an unexpected price. To escape they learn to rely on others, perhaps even to lead others, but at a price, they sacrifice they're self reliance, they need people now, even if only for company. A Blessing when manipulating someone into helping you or doing something they wouldn't ordinarily do gets one clarity. Curse, the Fairest loses clarity when she isolates herself, refusing help, or to rely on anyone.</div> </div> </div> </div>I actually have my own theory on this, but I think it's a little off-topic for this thread, so I'm going to make a separate thread for 2e Seeming predictions and discuss it there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-02T07:47:06-07:00","id":500341,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/498162-second-edition-darklings?p=500291#post500291\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm sorry, but I just totally disagree here. The Darklings never made much sense to me in 1e. The whole adaptable thing was not terribly interesting, and didn't follow through very well to why that made them creatures of darkness. If the new take on Kith and Seeming is that Kith is how your Keeper changed you and Seeming is how you changed yourself, than Darklings need to have made themselves darker to escape. Adaptability is just not dark, it's a pretty universally positive quality. Maybe the writeup focuses too much on loyalty and betrayal? I don't think so, but enough people seem to find it too narrow, so I guess that could be a way to improve. But I think it's important not to lose the fact that for someone to change themselves into a creature of the darkness in order to escape their Durance, they need to have had a light within them to begin with, and they need to have made the choice to let that light go out.</div> </div> </div> </div>YEAH, YOU TELL THEM CHARLY!<br /> <br /> Sorry, I got really excited.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-02T08:07:35-07:00","id":500357,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/498162-second-edition-darklings?p=500291#post500291\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm sorry, but I just totally disagree here. The Darklings never made much sense to me in 1e. The whole adaptable thing was not terribly interesting, and didn't follow through very well to why that made them creatures of darkness. If the new take on Kith and Seeming is that Kith is how your Keeper changed you and Seeming is how you changed yourself, than Darklings need to have made themselves darker to escape. Adaptability is just not dark, it's a pretty universally positive quality. Maybe the writeup focuses too much on loyalty and betrayal? I don't think so, but enough people seem to find it too narrow, so I guess that could be a way to improve. But I think it's important not to lose the fact that for someone to change themselves into a creature of the darkness in order to escape their Durance, they need to have had a light within them to begin with, and they need to have made the choice to let that light go out.</div> </div> </div> </div>Some fair comments. Perhaps Darklings SACRIFICE rather than adapt? Betraying seems inherently limiting to me and it seems a few others. I suppose a write up about Darklings betraying their better natures could fit but that seems awkward since betraying yourself doesn't have the same resonance as betraying others, but betraying others limits durances where the Darkling is totally isolated and alone. Sacrifice would allow characters that have snuffed out a light by external or internal means.<br /> <br /> Either way, I am going to reiterate that I think character concepts which read as more fairy-tale esqe would be nice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1161-gravitas-man","name":"Gravitas Man","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1161_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-02T08:38:17-07:00","id":500416,"title":"","content":"Betraying your values and principles is absolutely major.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-02T08:49:37-07:00","id":500458,"title":"","content":"Then I think the text would benefit in making that more obviously a viable interpretation. I personally would prefer sacrifice as the theme, but betraying yourself can work. My main concern is making as many character types possible for each seeming.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1161,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1161-gravitas-man","user":"Gravitas Man","date":".  Changed clunky sentance. 05-02-2015, 01:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1161-gravitas-man","name":"Gravitas Man","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1161_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-02T08:54:51-07:00","id":500461,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gravitas Man</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/498162-second-edition-darklings?p=500357#post500357\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Some fair comments. Perhaps Darklings SACRIFICE rather than adapt? Betraying seems inherently limiting to me and it seems a few others. I suppose a write up about Darklings betraying their better natures could fit but that seems awkward since betraying yourself doesn't have the same resonance as betraying others, but betraying others limits durances where the Darkling is totally isolated and alone. Sacrifice would allow characters that have snuffed out a light by external or internal means.<br /> <br /> Either way, I am going to reiterate that I think character concepts which read as more fairy-tale esqe would be nice.</div> </div> </div> </div>Personally, I read the betrayal thing as just one possible example or how a Darkling could have made themselves darker to escape. I guess that must not be clear enough in the writeup, because you're definitely not alone in finding it too limiting. If there were more word count available I would recommend keeping the current examples (both from the Darkling writeup and the Beast writeup) as sample characters and adding more on other ways that the good person turned dark or the restricted person turning wild narratives might express themselves.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-02T11:34:40-07:00","id":500552,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/498162-second-edition-darklings?p=500461#post500461\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally, I read the betrayal thing as just one possible example or how a Darkling could have made themselves darker to escape. I guess that must not be clear enough in the writeup, because you're definitely not alone in finding it too limiting.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm pretty sure the write up was edited to include qualifiers like &quot;many&quot; so for people like myself our first impressions were an even stronger focus on loyalty than you see now. That said; even with the changes I still think that having more examples of different ways a changeling can become a Darkling than just loyalty/betrayal would be a very big improvement. E.G. a priest who finds his Keeper's spellbook and goes against &quot;suffer not a witch to live&quot;.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-02T11:49:48-07:00","id":500578,"title":"","content":"There is something I am not understanding here, about Changeling 2E in general: why is self empowerment being equated to some sort of anti-social behavior? Is it just a theme of second edition that characters' attempts to regain self control are faulty because they are broken, scarred people, and can't relate healthily to people anymore? I remember the first edition as always being about clawing your way back from the edge with your recently escaped trauma looming over you, but this seems more that instead of trying to escape the pain the characters are rewarded for allowing themselves to be redefined by it. Is that kind of twisted outlook on purpose?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5428-mr-feral","name":"Mr. Feral","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5428_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-02T11:53:16-07:00","id":500582,"title":"","content":"It's a fair point Mr. Feral - but I wouldn't pass judgement until after we've seen all the Seemings.<br /> <br /> Also, the fact that Seemings are how you escaped is very important here. You're not defined by the trauma, but by the tools you developed to defeat the trauma. So long as there's one or two seemings that are pro-social it should be fine.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-02T12:01:19-07:00","id":500587,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr. Feral</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/498162-second-edition-darklings?p=500578#post500578\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is something I am not understanding here, about Changeling 2E in general: why is self empowerment being equated to some sort of anti-social behavior? Is it just a theme of second edition that characters' attempts to regain self control are faulty because they are broken, scarred people, and can't relate healthily to people anymore? I remember the first edition as always being about clawing your way back from the edge with your recently escaped trauma looming over you, but this seems more that instead of trying to escape the pain the characters are rewarded for allowing themselves to be redefined by it. Is that kind of twisted outlook on purpose?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think a Changeling is defined by her Seeming any more than a Vampire is defined by his Clan or a Werewolf is defined by his Auspice. It informs roleplay, but it doesn't define characters. You have to change yourself to escape your Durance, and that change may be for better or for worse, but either way it's going to have serious long-term impact on you. But that doesn't mean you have to let it rule you. You develop a new Breaking Point because you've been deeply traumatized and sometimes things are going to be triggering. You regain Clarity when you reaffirm your sense of self and the way the choices you made in order to escape fit within that identity. But beyond that, your Seeming doesn't control you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-02T12:02:37-07:00","id":500588,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr. Feral</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/498162-second-edition-darklings?p=500578#post500578\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is something I am not understanding here, about Changeling 2E in general: why is self empowerment being equated to some sort of anti-social behavior? Is it just a theme of second edition that characters' attempts to regain self control are faulty because they are broken, scarred people, and can't relate healthily to people anymore? I remember the first edition as always being about clawing your way back from the edge with your recently escaped trauma looming over you, but this seems more that instead of trying to escape the pain the characters are rewarded for allowing themselves to be redefined by it. Is that kind of twisted outlook on purpose?</div> </div> </div> </div>Now that you've made the point, this is largely while I feel the loyalty/betrayal dynamic, as currently written, comes across as too restrictive.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1161-gravitas-man","name":"Gravitas Man","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1161_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-02T12:09:51-07:00","id":500595,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr. Feral</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/498162-second-edition-darklings?p=500578#post500578\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is something I am not understanding here, about Changeling 2E in general: why is self empowerment being equated to some sort of anti-social behavior? Is it just a theme of second edition that characters' attempts to regain self control are faulty because they are broken, scarred people, and can't relate healthily to people anymore? I remember the first edition as always being about clawing your way back from the edge with your recently escaped trauma looming over you, but this seems more that instead of trying to escape the pain the characters are rewarded for allowing themselves to be redefined by it. Is that kind of twisted outlook on purpose?</div> </div> </div> </div>You aren't rewarded, you're changed. Trauma changes you whether you want it to or not. Faerie just takes those changes and makes them literal alterations of your physical body. The main difference now is that trauma comes from two sources. Kith, the things that were done to you, and Seeming, the things that you did. Much like the old court system mirrored the stages of grief, the new Seeming set-up seems to be building itself around the emotional problems that can result from PTSD.<br /> <br /> Crossposting from my stuff in the prediction thread:<br /> From what we've seen so far it seems like Seemings will be able to map pretty well with emotional issues that can arise from PTSD. Beasts act out, Darklings can't trust, Elementals are emotionally severed, Ogres &quot;consume&quot; which can translate to substance abuse or binging, Wizened look like they'll have a bit of a thing about modifying themselves or things around them so basically people who bury themselves in their work or something along those lines. As far as Fairest go, I'm expecting something involving either co-dependency or narcissism.<br /> -","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3738-illuminated-minutia","name":"Illuminated Minutia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3738_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-02T12:15:45-07:00","id":500599,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Illuminated Minutia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/498162-second-edition-darklings?p=500595#post500595\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From what we've seen so far it seems like Seemings will be able to map pretty well with emotional issues that can arise from PTSD.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pretty cool if it's true; but that makes me feel that overcoming those issues should be a valid Changeling story.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-02T12:24:51-07:00","id":500604,"title":"","content":"Oh absolutely. Working to manage your problems should a very big part of the story, but what's important about the current set up is that they are an issue <i>every</i> Changeling (with the possible exception of Loyalists and those who were freed) has to deal with and at the end of the day they will most likely never completely go away.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3738-illuminated-minutia","name":"Illuminated Minutia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3738_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-02T12:34:02-07:00","id":500607,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Illuminated Minutia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/498162-second-edition-darklings?p=500595#post500595\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Much like the old court system mirrored the stages of grief, the new Seeming set-up seems to be building itself around the emotional problems that can result from PTSD.<br /> -</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm completely fine with that as a concept. My concern (and I understand that I'm not seeing the book so I could be wrong) is that I don't see anything yet about overcoming these problems. The mechanics right now reinforce giving in to those unhealthy tendencies. Both gaining and losing clarity are based around the character's faulty mentalities.<br /> <br /> Also I am forced to agree that as written these descriptions are entirely too specific. They offer only a single interpretation of how a character ended up with a specific methodology. Yes, I can make a character that doesn't necessarily fit into that structure, but I don't see why it can't be written in a more general sense to begin with.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5428-mr-feral","name":"Mr. Feral","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5428_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-02T12:38:35-07:00","id":500613,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Illuminated Minutia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/498162-second-edition-darklings?p=500604#post500604\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">most likely never completely go away.</div> </div> </div> </div> &quot;most likely&quot; isn't &quot;always&quot; though.<br /> <br /> I think making those issues go away should be something all changelings can strive for, and make progress even if they don't completely remove the problems.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-02T12:38:38-07:00","id":500614,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gravitas Man</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/498162-second-edition-darklings?p=500588#post500588\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Now that you've made the point, this is largely while I feel the loyalty/betrayal dynamic, as currently written, comes across as too restrictive.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's just Darklings though. They're dark. It's right there in the name. Beasts are beastial. Elementals are elemental. Fairest are fair. Ogres are ogrish. Wizend are wize. If you don't like that Darklings are restricted to being dark, you might want to play a different Seeming.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-02T12:41:45-07:00","id":500616,"title":"","content":"It's not about them being dark; it's about them being one kind of dark when they should be every kind of dark.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-02T12:47:49-07:00","id":500638,"title":"","content":"There are so many possible reasons a character could end up devious, deceptive, or secretive. What I am failing to see is why the only one presented is this specific sense of betrayal from this specific interaction. Especially because as an analogy it is worrisome: that the way to react to one person hurting you is to internalize it and act viciously to others for your entire life. The same thing could happen to a character and they could easily be a fairest or wizened or anything else depending on how they react.<br /> <br /> Just to suggest &quot;this isn't the seeming for you&quot; ignores the problem. I want to be a darkling, but who I see as a darkling. Not someone else's interpretation. This is about taking these ideas and giving your players the chance to be creative.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5428,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5428-mr-feral","user":"Mr. Feral","date":". 05-02-2015, 03:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5428-mr-feral","name":"Mr. Feral","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5428_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-02T12:59:44-07:00","id":500658,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/498162-second-edition-darklings?p=500616#post500616\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's not about them being dark; it's about them being one kind of dark when they should be every kind of dark.</div> </div> </div> </div>Could you give me an example of a Darkling character concept that doesn't fit within this portrayal of Darklings as people who are taken advantage of due to their &quot;light&quot; and change themselves into a darker person to end that cycle?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-02T13:07:46-07:00","id":500676,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr. Feral</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/498162-second-edition-darklings?p=500638#post500638\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are so many possible reasons a character could end up devious, deceptive, or secretive. What I am failing to see is why the only one presented is this specific sense of betrayal from this specific interaction. Especially because as an analogy it is worrisome: that the way to react to one person hurting you is to internalize it and act viciously to others for your entire life. The same thing could happen to a character and they could easily be a fairest or wizened or anything else depending on how they react.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm pretty sure the specific narrative in this writeup is meant as just one example. But what Seeming represents in 2e is how you changed yourself to escape your Durance. Sure, a Wizened or a Fairest could have had similar experiences of betrayal and reacted to them differently - that's why they're different Seemings. They changed themselves in different ways.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr. Feral</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/498162-second-edition-darklings?p=500638#post500638\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just to suggest &quot;this isn't the seeming for you&quot; ignores the problem. I want to be a darkling, but who I see as a darkling. Not someone else's interpretation. This is about taking these ideas and giving your players the chance to be creative.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, as long as the way you see a Darkling fits within the (pretty minimal) constraints given here, you should be fine. That is to say, being in situations where they have to put complete trust in another is triggering to them, and making tough calls reaffirms their sense of agency. If your character concept doesn't fit within those constraints, it's not a Darkling. Just like a vampire who doesn't become obsessively attached to their blood dolls isn't a Daeva.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-02T14:17:11-07:00","id":500770,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/498162-second-edition-darklings?p=500658#post500658\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Could you give me an example of a Darkling character concept that doesn't fit within this portrayal of Darklings as people who are taken advantage of due to their &quot;light&quot; and change themselves into a darker person to end that cycle?</div> </div> </div> </div>I've already posted several examples in this thread. For example:<br /> <br /> Bob Average was no more loyal than your average man, and suffered no greater betrayals than the average man. One day for completely random reasons he was abducted and set to back breaking work in the mines. Then by accident he dug his way into an old vault and found a spellbook; unfortunately the spell of invisiblity required a human/changeling heart; so he killed someone and used their heart to turn invisible and escape.<br /> <br /> <br /> No loyalty. No being taken advantage off (unless you count the Keeper). However committing cold blooded murder is without a doubt becoming a darker person.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-02T14:19:44-07:00","id":500773,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/498162-second-edition-darklings?p=500770#post500770\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've already posted several examples in this thread. For example:<br /> <br /> Bob Average was no more loyal than your average man, and suffered no greater betrayals than the average man. One day for completely random reasons he was abducted and set to back breaking work in the mines. Then by accident he dug his way into an old vault and found a spellbook; unfortunately the spell of invisiblity required a human/changeling heart; so he killed someone and used their heart to turn invisible and escape.<br /> <br /> No loyalty. No being taken advantage off (unless you count the Keeper). However committing cold blooded murder is without a doubt becoming a darker person.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't see any part of that not fitting within the framework of the writeup. He may not be a typical example, but he sure sounds like a 2e Darkling to me.<br /> <br /> EDIT: And yes, I do count his Keeper. That's exactly what I'm talking about when I say his &quot;light&quot; makes him an easy victim. That's what lead to him being taken, just like in 1e they were taken because of some sort of transgression.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 05-02-2015, 05:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-02T15:11:37-07:00","id":500805,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/498162-second-edition-darklings?p=500773#post500773\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't see any part of that not fitting within the framework of the writeup. He may not be a typical example, but he sure sounds like a 2e Darkling to me.</div> </div> </div> </div> There's nothing in the write up that explicitly rejects this charachter. But there's also nothing that explicitly supports it.<br /> <br /> There is lots that explicitly supports someone who was a loyal person pre-durance and who's motivation for their escape plan was being &quot;abandoned&quot; during the durance.<br /> <br /> That is why I would say it doesn't &quot;fit&quot;. It's not excluded, it's just not included.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/498162-second-edition-darklings?p=500773#post500773\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's exactly what I'm talking about when I say his &quot;light&quot; makes him an easy victim. That's what lead to him being taken</div> </div> </div> </div> What on Earth? Where did you get this from?<br /> <br /> There is <b>nothing</b> that makes him an easy victim because Joe Average intentionally has no traits that can make him an easier victim than the average person. (or any traits at all)<br /> <br /> His &quot;light&quot; didn't lead to him getting taken. I explictly said he was taken for completely random reasons precisely to make the point that you can become a Darkling completely independently of why your keeper chose you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 05-02-2015, 06:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-02T15:44:19-07:00","id":500853,"title":"","content":"But why is who the character was before the taking even a part of the Kith/seeming system? Isn't the entire point the way you <i>react</i> to trauma? Who you are beforehand does influence that, but a person can go in many different directions based on their experiences as much as their predispositions. I resent the idea that a kith not only helps me describe who my character is, but who they always used to be. What if I want that to be unclear? What if I want it to be hazy and unclear and his arc to be about discovering why who he used to be is different from who he is?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5428-mr-feral","name":"Mr. Feral","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5428_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-02T15:52:44-07:00","id":500859,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr. Feral</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/498162-second-edition-darklings?p=500853#post500853\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But why is who the character was before the taking even a part of the Kith/seeming system? Isn't the entire point the way you <i>react</i> to trauma? Who you are beforehand does influence that, but a person can go in many different directions based on their experiences as much as their predispositions. I resent the idea that a kith not only helps me describe who my character is, but who they always used to be. What if I want that to be unclear? What if I want it to be hazy and unclear and his arc to be about discovering why who he used to be is different from who he is?</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree with this. Now that I've given it some thought, I would much prefer to see background sections kept as vague as possible, maybe a sentance or two, with the rest of the words devoted to the seeming overall.<br /> <br /> As for a Darkling character that doesn't fit the current dynamic very clearly, I point you to Baron Samedi's excellent Actual Play.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filedataid=1074\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\"> Changeling: Malibu Dream House (Actual Play) - Onyx Path Forums </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\"> http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> https://s19.postimg.org/mq7syxicz/Pic_Sheet1.jpg https://s19.postimg.org/ous600rpf/Pic_Sheet2.jpg Changeling: Malibu Dream House is a Changeling: The Lost </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> The character of Insincere Marguerite.<br /> <br /> Perhaps this is a case of the reversal of Kith/Seeming and in 2e the character would be a Tunnelgrub Fairest or some such but as it stands, it doesn't clealy fit the new mould.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1161,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1161-gravitas-man","user":"Gravitas Man","date":". 05-02-2015, 06:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1161-gravitas-man","name":"Gravitas Man","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1161_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-02T16:05:26-07:00","id":500871,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/498162-second-edition-darklings?p=500805#post500805\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> There's nothing in the write up that explicitly rejects this charachter. But there's also nothing that explicitly supports it.<br /> <br /> There is lots that explicitly supports someone who was a loyal person pre-durance and who's motivation for their escape plan was being &quot;abandoned&quot; during the durance.<br /> <br /> That is why I would say it doesn't &quot;fit&quot;. It's not excluded, it's just not included.</div> </div> </div> </div>I just don't expect most concepts to be explicitly provided for in the example, I guess. If it fits, go for it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/498162-second-edition-darklings?p=500805#post500805\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What on Earth? Where did you get this from?<br /> <br /> There is <b>nothing</b> that makes him an easy victim because Joe Average intentionally has no traits that can make him an easier victim than the average person. (or any traits at all)<br /> <br /> His &quot;light&quot; didn't lead to him getting taken. I explictly said he was taken for completely random reasons precisely to make the point that you can become a Darkling completely independently of why your keeper chose you.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry, I did not make myself clear. Your character not having that vulnerability is what makes him atypical in my mind. Otherwise, he seems perfectly Darkling. What I was trying to say is that all Changelings are taken advantage of by their Keeper, and the Kith backgrounds are examples of what kind of character would be vulnerable to that, and likely to escape in such a way that causes them to be become that Seeming. Just like not all 1e Darklings were taken because of a transgression of some kind, not all 2e Darklings were taken because they were loyal or trusting. But that is the typical narrative, which is why it's described in the example.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-02T17:19:42-07:00","id":500995,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/498162-second-edition-darklings?p=500770#post500770\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've already posted several examples in this thread. For example:<br /> <br /> Bob Average was no more loyal than your average man, and suffered no greater betrayals than the average man. One day for completely random reasons he was abducted and set to back breaking work in the mines. Then by accident he dug his way into an old vault and found a spellbook; unfortunately the spell of invisiblity required a human/changeling heart; so he killed someone and used their heart to turn invisible and escape.<br /> <br /> <br /> No loyalty. No being taken advantage off (unless you count the Keeper). However committing cold blooded murder is without a doubt becoming a darker person.</div> </div> </div> </div>However, IMO, that character becomes much richer if you add those elements. Who did that heart come from? Was it REALLY an accident that he dug in there, or did someone want to see him in that situation? <br /> <br /> With any character, the less you describe them in relationship to the world around them, and the more you genericize them as an example, the more you're going to find &quot;this isn't specifically included.&quot; Examples in the prose aren't going to be about Bob Average, because he's Bob Average.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-02T17:32:19-07:00","id":501012,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr. Feral</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/498162-second-edition-darklings?p=500853#post500853\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But why is who the character was before the taking even a part of the Kith/seeming system? Isn't the entire point the way you <i>react</i> to trauma? Who you are beforehand does influence that, but a person can go in many different directions based on their experiences as much as their predispositions. I resent the idea that a kith not only helps me describe who my character is, but who they always used to be. What if I want that to be unclear? What if I want it to be hazy and unclear and his arc to be about discovering why who he used to be is different from who he is?</div> </div> </div> </div>Then do that. Not every character has to fit with the example. But examples of typical backgrounds for characters of a given X-splat are nothing new. They've been a part of every line for over 10 years, why is it suddenly a problem now?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-02T17:32:37-07:00","id":501014,"title":"","content":"The above. In hindsight, I think the reason I'm reacting strongly against making it more broad is the worry it will become too broad and... flavorless. <br /> <br /> Yes, there's probably a way to make it more broad that doesn't suck out flavor, however even those isn't going ever be as broad, I'd argue, as losing any type of virtue. Especially as we're assuming the other Seemings don't also somehow involve say, losing a part of your moral code in the manner Darklings do. <br /> <br /> That, and Bob Average makes a rather boring example.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1657-killer300","name":"Killer300","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"216"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-02T17:42:31-07:00","id":501025,"title":"","content":"All forms of Darkness invovle some kind of Betrayal, it could be a Betrayal of Family, betraying friends, betraying strangers, betraying your self, betraying your beliefs, betraying your country, betraying the Gentry, ect... Sometimes life gives you only the choice of who to Betray. There is no Darkling story that can't fit under this theme.<br /> <br /> I really don't want this really cool Seeming watered down to the point that it loses all depth, and everything that makes it exciting to explore, in the name of making it as flavourlessly generic as possible, I don't think its needed, honestly my fear is they drop the awesome background section, and just turn it into generic emo seeming, moody and brooding, beings who did something bad at some point to escape.<br /> <br /> I'm willing to comprise, leave in the background, but make it clear that they're are exceptions to it.<br /> <br /> I really don't want the best awesomest parts of the Darkling cut out so the Darkling becomes watered down, I've seen that sort of thing happen before and it doesn't work out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-02T17:43:45-07:00","id":501026,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/498162-second-edition-darklings?p=500995#post500995\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> However, IMO, that character becomes much richer if you add those elements. Who did that heart come from? Was it REALLY an accident that he dug in there, or did someone want to see him in that situation? <br /> <br /> With any character, the less you describe them in relationship to the world around them, and the more you genericize them as an example, the more you're going to find &amp;quot;this isn't specifically included.&amp;quot; Examples in the prose aren't going to be about Bob Average, because he's Bob Average.</div> </div> </div> </div> I agree 110%","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-02T17:59:56-07:00","id":501032,"title":"","content":"I think what I am saying here is being deeply misunderstood, as is the process of crafting these archetypes itself. What I want is a description of the defining features, not specific events. You can tell me a darkling is untrustworthy, duplicitous, and given to trusting his judgment over that of others and I can draw my own conclusions. The mechanical lattice supports and informs my character choices. These things can both be described by generalities and have a consistent theme. I don't see why you feel the need to draw the firm line in the sand that either a character is precisely one version of a mindset or a bland, meaningless caricature.<br /> <br /> People become jaded and self-reliant for many reasons other than betrayal, but even if you want to say the theme is that of betrayal, it can be done while still making clear that there are many divergent types. I want the chance to breathe my own life into the character I create, not have that life given to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5428-mr-feral","name":"Mr. Feral","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5428_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-02T18:07:08-07:00","id":501049,"title":"","content":"Nothing in the write up says Darklings have to be mean vicious people, the majority aren't sociopaths, they care, they care enough to take the burden of needed betrays upon themselves so as to spare the inner light of others, and this leaves them scared and untrusting, most don't act cruelly for no reason or all the time. Not to say every thing they do is selfless, just that nothing stops them from acts of kindness, a Darkling Windwing could.decide to fly up to the top of a tall tree to save a trapped scared kitten, just as much as any other seeming. But trust comes hard and usually with strings attached, and they're practical ruthlessness and guarded nature means they sometimes make choices of a morally questionable or even straight up bad nature, sometimes.<br /> <br /> Good examples of Darkling, Frank Underwood (House of Cards), Sarah Walker (Chuck), John Casey (Chuck), Hiezenberg (Breaking Bad), Garak (DS9), Agent Sloan (DS9), Dexter Morgan (Dexter), Debra Morgan (Dexter), Seska (Voyager), Ensign Ro (TNG), Lauren (Lost Girl ironic as one of the none fae on the show), Trick (Lost Girl), Vex (Lost Girl), The Morrigan (Lost Girl).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-02T18:14:21-07:00","id":501067,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gravitas Man</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/498162-second-edition-darklings?p=500859#post500859\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for a Darkling character that doesn't fit the current dynamic very clearly, I point you to Baron Samedi's excellent Actual Play.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filedataid=1074\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\"> Changeling: Malibu Dream House (Actual Play) - Onyx Path Forums </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\"> http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> https://s19.postimg.org/mq7syxicz/Pic_Sheet1.jpg https://s19.postimg.org/ous600rpf/Pic_Sheet2.jpg Changeling: Malibu Dream House is a Changeling: The Lost </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> The character of Insincere Marguerite.<br /> <br /> Perhaps this is a case of the reversal of Kith/Seeming and in 2e the character would be a Tunnelgrub Fairest or some such but as it stands, it doesn't clealy fit the new mould.</div> </div> </div> </div> Forgive me being somewhat pedantic, but Marguerite wouldn't have a Seeming at all, because her Keeper set her free instead of her escaping on her own.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-02T18:34:55-07:00","id":501112,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr. Feral</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/498162-second-edition-darklings?p=501032#post501032\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think what I am saying here is being deeply misunderstood, as is the process of crafting these archetypes itself. What I want is a description of the defining features, not specific events. You can tell me a darkling is untrustworthy, duplicitous, and given to trusting his judgment over that of others and I can draw my own conclusions. The mechanical lattice supports and informs my character choices. These things can both be described by generalities and have a consistent theme. I don't see why you feel the need to draw the firm line in the sand that either a character is precisely one version of a mindset or a bland, meaningless caricature.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think anyone is trying to say that. I think some of us just identify very strongly with this very accurate depiction of a particular abuse survivor narrative - without getting to personal here, this story rings very true to me, and from what Omegaphallic has said, presumably to them as well. We just don't want to lose that just so more concepts can be made to fit the Seeming.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr. Feral</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/498162-second-edition-darklings?p=501032#post501032\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">People become jaded and self-reliant for many reasons other than betrayal, but even if you want to say the theme is that of betrayal, it can be done while still making clear that there are many divergent types. I want the chance to breathe my own life into the character I create, not have that life given to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>When I read this writeup, I don't see &quot;Darklings are Jaded and self-reliant.&quot; I see an all too familiar narrative about someone who is preyed upon because they are too trusting, or too loyal, or too generous, and the only way they can escape from that is to change their attitude, to accept that what they thought was just &quot;doing the right thing&quot; was making them a target for that abuse, that it will only end if they change their habits. And even once they've gotten free, it still affects them for the rest of their lives. They have difficulty putting their faith in others because they've done that before and it got them hurt. They find comfort in their newfound power to do what needs to be done, even when it may not seem like &quot;the right thing to do&quot; because they've seen what &quot;doing the right thing&quot; can lead to. <br /> <br /> Now there are a LOT of ways this particular story can play out. If your character concept doesn't fit within that narrative, you should very seriously consider the possibility that that character is a different Seeming, because they have evidently not experienced the same kind of trauma that leads one to become a Darkling.<br /> <br /> Could the writeup stand to have more varied examples? Sure. I didn't feel that need because I immediately identified with what someone in this kind of narrative goes through, but I can certainly see the value in giving more examples for others who don't identify with it as intuitively. I could even get behind broadening some of the language to make it more clear that this is one way the story might go, but not the only way. But I definitely do not want this incredibly powerful look into one means of a victim reclaiming agency to be watered down so it can accommodate stories that don't actually fit this very real abuse survivor narrative.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 05-02-2015, 09:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-02T18:40:32-07:00","id":501123,"title":"","content":"Murdering someone for thier heart is just as much turning your back on humanity, its the act of a predator and a violation of humanity's conventions and taboos, so Bob Average could just as easily become a Beast. <br /> <br /> or one could look at Bob Average like this, Bob was born into a good Jewish Family, and raised with deep seated religious values. He got kidnapped by his keeper for his dedication to hard work and made to serve in the mines. <br /> <br /> While mining, he awaited rescue from the being Bob was certain was the devil, but nothing happened. Bob felt abadoned by God when he found the book with the invisiblity spell, buried in a chest in the earth.<br /> <br /> It required a still beating heart from a living changeling. Bob didn't want to do such a horrible thing, but God had abaddoned him, and Bob couldn't handle it anymore he just couldn't take the suffering and hopelessness of his enslavement. <br /> <br /> The Question was how to create the opportunity to harvest the heart needed for the ritual, the tunnels were crowded and often tight. <br /> <br /> Bob befriended the friendliest person there, a young man named Eric. One day Bob convinced Eric he had a way out and he wanted to take him with him, taking the young man into the tunnel.where Bob kept the book.<br /> <br /> Bob murdered the hopeful and excited young men, tears dripping down Bob face as he heard Eric's last painful sobs before finally dying. Bob knew it had been needful, its was the only way out and Eric had no future, but suffering anyways, but Bob vomitted anyways.<br /> <br /> He then took Eric's Heart, glazing into and chanting the spell. As its turned to dust and turned Bob invisible, it revealed it secret to Bob had a vision of Eric as a young man holding a baby boy when a Darkness tried to steal him away. <br /> <br /> Eric intervene to protect the baby and was kidnapped instead, and only for the Darkness to leave a false copy of Eric behind. Bob recognized the room, its was his as a child. Bob had just murdered his own father, cruelly hacking his chest open to steal his heart, in order to save himself. His father hadn't aged a day since his kidnapping.<br /> <br /> Choking back his tears and shame, Bob fled the tunnels, fled Arcadia, and fought through the thorns of the hedge to get back to earth, the thorns tearing at his flesh, shaping it until his body matched the stains on his soul.<br /> <br /> Now which Bob Average would you want to play, Captain Generic, or Bob &quot;Patricide&quot; Average?<br /> <br /> Generic isn't a virtue.<br /> <br /> Also every Seeming can do bad things in escaping. Heck if all it took was doing something bad to get free, all Loyalists would be Darklings.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-02T19:08:30-07:00","id":501205,"title":"","content":"While I am starting to believe that Charlaquin and I are having a minor disagreement based on some different readings of the material and diverging thoughts on theme, Omegaphallic you appear to have entirely missed what I am attempting to get at. I never said generic is a virtue or that I want to play a character with no life or history. Reading what I have written shows that I want exactly that from my characters. I am also fine with an example member of a kith/seeming to show how one of these might be created. However, granting a single, highly specific character, such as Mr. Patricide, locks down options. There is an enormous, vibrant place in between Captain Generic and a single previously defined character.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5428-mr-feral","name":"Mr. Feral","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5428_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-02T19:18:10-07:00","id":501214,"title":"","content":"Okay is what some people who have problem with the Darkling about the example characters or something, I'm confused now, because they are three very different examples at the end.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-02T19:54:46-07:00","id":501247,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/498162-second-edition-darklings?p=501214#post501214\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay is what some people who have problem with the Darkling about the example characters or something, I'm confused now, because they are three very different examples at the end.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, I believe the problem some people are having is that between the &quot;background&quot; section and the &quot;the escape&quot; section, the writeup describes a very specific chain of events: a loyal person is betrayed, that sends them running to the arms of her keeper, then one of her fellow prisoners makes their escape, abandoning her in the process, then she does the same to someone else in the process of her own escape. As I understand it, they want it to be more clear that this is not the only way to become a Darkling.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-02T21:10:51-07:00","id":501331,"title":"","content":"Hi. I'm the writer. Just wanted to drop some thoughts: Please keep in mind first and foremost, that this is a first draft, and I can and will tighten the language. Thank you for the input. <br /> <br /> 1)I was very careful to say 'many' and 'most' or ever 'some' in the text. I talked about trends not absolutes. Take a look, it's in there. I did plot out a specific skeleton for players to build their own flesh on to, but how many arms, legs, heads, all that stuff, that's on you. I also, because I'm talking about trends, want you to know that you don't have to use my skeleton in whole.<br /> <br /> 2)Why make it so specific instead of something more generic? Because I'm a professional writer and I want to tell stories with my work. If you don't want to use my story starters, you don't have to. I'm not going to come to your home and tell you that Murder Mc Loves No One is officially 'NOT A DARKLING' and burn your books. I don't care what you do with it at your table, I care that what I put in the book is evocative, tantalising, and inspirational. That means being less generic. If you look over the thread, you'll see that many people are inspired by the specificity here. And we're all adults (I hope) so of course we're all aware that everyone is going to take the parts they like and chunk the rest. That's kinda what gamers do.<br /> <br /> 3)If you REALLY want me to make more generic material, my rate is 5 cents a word, half up front, half on turn over of the second draft. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <br /> <br /> I can answer more specific questions if you want, but I don't want to spend too much time here because I'd rather be working on game material than answering the same six questions over and over, yanno?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/184-filamena","name":"Filamena","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar184_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-02T22:04:18-07:00","id":501363,"title":"","content":"And now I must play Murder McLovesnoone.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-02T23:57:39-07:00","id":501447,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/498162-second-edition-darklings?p=500871#post500871\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just don't expect most concepts to be explicitly provided for in the example, I guess. If it fits, go for it.</div> </div> </div> </div> Neither do I.<br /> <br /> But a write up that gives three different example concept is a lot more welcoming concepts aren't explicitly mentioned than a write up that only mentions one example. Have a look back at page 6 to see how I'd do this write up.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/498162-second-edition-darklings?p=500871#post500871\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But that is the typical narrative, which is why it's described in the example.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which I disagree with quite strongly.<br /> <br /> I don't think there is or should be <b>any</b> typical narrative. Each Darkling should have their own narrative.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/498162-second-edition-darklings?p=500995#post500995\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">However, IMO, that character becomes much richer if you add those elements. Who did that heart come from? Was it REALLY an accident that he dug in there, or did someone want to see him in that situation?<br /> <br /> With any character, the less you describe them in relationship to the world around them, and the more you genericize them as an example, the more you're going to find &quot;this isn't specifically included.&quot; Examples in the prose aren't going to be about Bob Average, because he's Bob Average.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well naturally. Bob Average was written to prove a point to Charlaquin, he was not written to be a good charachter; so naturally he's not a great charachter.<br /> <br /> If you dig through the thread you'll see that I've also used examples that IMO are good charachters, like this one who'll I'll expand upon:<br /> <br /> Father Peter was a young vicar assigned to a rural parish. Like many priests he made a point of being interested in the local community and history, which is why he decided to take a walk and see the local sites, including a forest grove with many folklore tales about it. Those folk tales had a basis in truth: the True Fae saw him visiting and stole Peter away to toil in the mines.<br /> <br /> During his Durance Peter would preach to his fellow slaves after every day of back breaking labour, until the day he accidently dug into an old vault and found a magic wand with one charge left. Giving into temptation he used the wand to turn himself invisible and escape. However witchcraft is a sin, and though he is free Peter believes himself damned. Because he gave up on his faith, he considers himself damned.<br /> <br /> You could squeeze some talk of loyalty and abandonment out of this charachter. But clearly - to father Peter his faith and his sin are the core issue.<br /> <br /> ====================<br /> <br /> My issue with the write up isn't that there's nothing explicitly saying giving up your faith is on the &quot;big list of Darkling origins&quot;. It's that <u><b>all</b></u> the text about Darkling backstories is loyalty and abandonment.<br /> <br /> Having only one example origin makes it feel like that's the cannonical origin and anything else is a weird edge case. Having three examples makes it feel like there's hundreds of potential origins and you get to see a few examples.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/498162-second-edition-darklings?p=501112#post501112\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think anyone is trying to say that. I think some of us just identify very strongly with this very accurate depiction of a particular abuse survivor narrative - without getting to personal here, this story rings very true to me, and from what Omegaphallic has said, presumably to them as well. We just don't want to lose that just so more concepts can be made to fit the Seeming.</div> </div> </div> </div>In this thread not one person ever said this example Darkspawn should be lost. We're just saying that he shouldn't be presented as though he was the default Darkling.<br /> <br /> He could be condensed down to fewer words to make room for other options, he could be made into a sample charachter, he could be moved into opening fiction.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/498162-second-edition-darklings?p=501112#post501112\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> to accept that what they thought was just &quot;doing the right thing&quot; was making them a target for that abuse</div> </div> </div> </div> Now this I disagree with. I don't think a Darkling needs to believe that doing the right thing was what made them a target.<br /> <br /> They just need to believe that doing the right thing would have prevented their escape.<br /> <br /> Both Bob Average and Father Peter weren't targeted because they did the right thing. Bob Average was random, Father Peter was just in the wrong place at the wrong time. You could add a third example of someone who was abducted for eating a faerie's food then escaped with Bob's ritual.<br /> <br /> However if they did the right thing they wouldn't have escaped. If Bob did the right thing he'd have decided not to cut out someone's heart. If Peter did what he believed to be the right thing he'd never have sinned by using witchcraft. As a result both would have remained slaves.<br /> <br /> Both decided to do the wrong thing, and from that they learned a life lesson. They'd do the wrong thing again if it was &quot;nessacary&quot;.<br /> <br /> A Darkling who was enslaved because of a virtue and who decided they'd never let that virtue be a &quot;weakness&quot; again is a great charachter, but it should not be portrayed over the default over a charachter who was abducted for an unrelated reason.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/498162-second-edition-darklings?p=501123#post501123\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Murdering someone for thier heart is just as much turning your back on humanity, its the act of a predator and a violation of humanity's conventions and taboos, so Bob Average could just as easily become a Beast.</div> </div> </div> </div>By that standard, the current Darkling write up could result in a Beast. Loyalty is a human convention and betrayal is a human taboo.<br /> <br /> (Which btw I approve off. The fact that your Seeming is partly what you did, and partly how you felt about what you did, is something I like)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 05-03-2015, 03:18 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-03T00:03:57-07:00","id":501451,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/498162-second-edition-darklings?p=501447#post501447\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Neither do I.<br /> <br /> But a write up that gives three different example concept is a lot more welcoming concepts aren't explicitly mentioned than a write up that only mentions one example. Have a look back at page 6 to see how I'd do this write up.<br /> <br /> Which I disagree with quite strongly.<br /> <br /> I don't think there is or should be <b>any</b> typical narrative. Each Darkling should have their own narrative.<br /> <br /> Well naturally. Bob Average was written to prove a point to Charlaquin, he was not written to be a good charachter; so naturally he's not a great charachter.<br /> <br /> If you dig through the thread you'll see that I've also used examples that IMO are good charachters, like this one who'll I'll expand upon:<br /> <br /> Father Peter was a young vicar assigned to a rural parish. Like many priests he made a point of being interested in the local community and history, which is why he decided to take a walk and see the local sites, including a forest grove with many folklore tales about it. Those folk tales had a basis in truth: the True Fae saw him visiting and stole Peter away to toil in the mines.<br /> <br /> During his Durance Peter would preach to his fellow slaves after every day of back breaking labour, until the day he accidently dug into an old vault and found a magic wand with one charge left. Giving into temptation he used the wand to turn himself invisible and escape. However witchcraft is a sin, and though he is free Peter believes himself damned. Because he gave up on his faith, he considers himself damned.<br /> <br /> ====================<br /> <br /> My issue with the write up isn't that there's nothing explicitly saying giving up your faith is on the &quot;big list of Darkling origins&quot;. It's that <u><b>all</b></u> the text about Darkling backstories is loyalty and abandonment.<br /> <br /> Having only one example origin makes it feel like that's the cannonical origin and anything else is a weird edge case. Having three examples makes it feel like there's hundreds of potential origins and you get to see a few examples.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, the later example won me, somewhat, over to your point. That and...<br /> <br /> I'm really starting to see your point because of the Fairest. Its... an odd realization to have. Granted, that's a case of an Archetype dominating, but, that's another matter.<br /> <br /> With this said, I'm very adamant about avoiding excessive breadth, as I'd argue that can suck out all flavor from a Seeming.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1657,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1657-killer300","user":"Killer300","date":". 05-03-2015, 03:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1657-killer300","name":"Killer300","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"216"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-03T11:07:46-07:00","id":501912,"title":"","content":"Religious faith is hugely about loyalty, most religious people would concider the Preachers behavoir a breach of loyalty to the Christian God.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-03T11:57:47-07:00","id":501966,"title":"","content":"Not Father Peter. He's an Anglican, so basically atheist. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I kid. but you have a point - however it's a point about the example rather than the issue itself. Bob Average didn't have that loyalty, neither did the golddigger I mentioned earlier unthread.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 05-03-2015, 03:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-03T12:27:14-07:00","id":502004,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/498162-second-edition-darklings?p=501966#post501966\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not Father Peter. He's an Anglican, so basically atheist. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I kid. but you have a point - however it's a point about the example rather than the issue itself. Bob Average didn't have that loyalty, neither did the golddigger I mentioned earlier unthread.</div> </div> </div> </div>And the gold digger was a terrible example, mostly because I'd argue that the Keeper isn't going to let her, if you will, have access to opportunities where she could use those skills to escape. I know that has issues, but you mentioned upthread your issues with the destiny thing is it makes it Keeper controlled, one of them anyway, however this falls into the same trap. Why would the Keeper let a gold digger into situation where she can exploit those skills?<br /> <br /> She's more likely to become a different Seeming from having different opportunities, and a different way of gaining agency.<br /> <br /> Even if she was going to become a Darkling, I'd argue it'd have to be through a route that isn't dependent on your prior skill set, which... would still probably involve loyalty to something, it just wouldn't be her prior husbands.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1657,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1657-killer300","user":"Killer300","date":". 05-03-2015, 03:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1657-killer300","name":"Killer300","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"216"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-03T12:35:40-07:00","id":502035,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Filamena</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/498162-second-edition-darklings?p=501331#post501331\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hi. I'm the writer. Just wanted to drop some thoughts: Please keep in mind first and foremost, that this is a first draft, and I can and will tighten the language. Thank you for the input.<br /> <br /> 1)I was very careful to say 'many' and 'most' or ever 'some' in the text. I talked about trends not absolutes. Take a look, it's in there. I did plot out a specific skeleton for players to build their own flesh on to, but how many arms, legs, heads, all that stuff, that's on you. I also, because I'm talking about trends, want you to know that you don't have to use my skeleton in whole.<br /> <br /> 2)Why make it so specific instead of something more generic? Because I'm a professional writer and I want to tell stories with my work. If you don't want to use my story starters, you don't have to. I'm not going to come to your home and tell you that Murder Mc Loves No One is officially 'NOT A DARKLING' and burn your books. I don't care what you do with it at your table, I care that what I put in the book is evocative, tantalising, and inspirational. That means being less generic. If you look over the thread, you'll see that many people are inspired by the specificity here. And we're all adults (I hope) so of course we're all aware that everyone is going to take the parts they like and chunk the rest. That's kinda what gamers do.<br /> <br /> 3)If you REALLY want me to make more generic material, my rate is 5 cents a word, half up front, half on turn over of the second draft. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I can answer more specific questions if you want, but I don't want to spend too much time here because I'd rather be working on game material than answering the same six questions over and over, yanno?</div> </div> </div> </div>I take issue with the notion that if I don't play your very specific idea of what a Darkling is, I must be necessity be playing Murder McLovesNoOne. I am not asking for generic material and I never was. I recognize that as a writer you want your story to be told, but that's the problem here: these games are to let the players and storytellers...well...tell their own story. I'm not saying what you have is badly written, off point, or even a bad darkling. I'm not saying that it is the only conceivable type of character and you leave NO room for anything else. All I am asking for is that it be made more clear that there are other options and what some of them might be, rather than shunting us into a single idea of what makes someone a darkling. Also isn't the purpose of putting these notes up is for feedback. Why is it offensive to suggest that changes be made to the point where you ask payment of the fans (who, by the way, DO support you by purchasing the products, offering feedback, and generally enjoying these games).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5428-mr-feral","name":"Mr. Feral","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5428_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-03T12:40:22-07:00","id":502039,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr. Feral</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/498162-second-edition-darklings?p=502035#post502035\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I take issue with the notion that if I don't play your very specific idea of what a Darkling is, I must be necessity be playing Murder McLovesNoOne. I am not asking for generic material and I never was. I recognize that as a writer you want your story to be told, but that's the problem here: these games are to let the players and storytellers...well...tell their own story. I'm not saying what you have is badly written, off point, or even a bad darkling. I'm not saying that it is the only conceivable type of character and you leave NO room for anything else. All I am asking for is that it be made more clear that there are other options and what some of them might be, rather than shunting us into a single idea of what makes someone a darkling. Also isn't the purpose of putting these notes up is for feedback. Why is it offensive to suggest that changes be made to the point where you ask payment of the fans (who, by the way, DO support you by purchasing the products, offering feedback, and generally enjoying these games).</div> </div> </div> </div>Is it though? The wording I think leaves it quite clear, and the exceptions... well, are that, exceptions to be worked out at the table. <br /> <br /> That, and I just don't how the loyalty concept is that restrictive in of itself. More than that, as I've said earlier, there have to be a few... constraints(restrictions is too harsh), on thematic elements in a Seeming. Otherwise, a write up for a Seeming would become flavorless from being far too broad. <br /> <br /> There may be a better middle ground, but its probably not going to be anywhere near as broad as some in the thread seem to want it to be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1657-killer300","name":"Killer300","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"216"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-03T12:42:53-07:00","id":502046,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Killer300</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/498162-second-edition-darklings?p=502004#post502004\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And the gold digger was a terrible example, mostly because I'd argue that the Keeper isn't going to let her, if you will, have access to opportunities where she could use those skills to escape.</div> </div> </div> </div> Um what?<br /> <br /> Any Durance where that gold digger has the oppotunity to talk to men would be an oppotunity.<br /> <br /> Heck, you're assuming that the Keeper chose her for her skills and choose a durance because of that. He might have chose her for her looks, or because she ate his food (he left it lying around on Earth by mistake). Her durance might be completely unrelated to her skills. <br /> <br /> Lets say that she ate some of his food and in return he sets her to work in the mines (my favourite example) she's working side by side with men, so she could seduce one and convince him to attack the guards - knowing that he'll die - so she can escape in the commotion.<br /> <br /> She wasn't abandoned, she wasn't loyal before or during her Durance. She's still a Darkling, intentionally getting someone killed is pretty Dark (and we now know it's certainly not Fairest).<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-03T12:59:18-07:00","id":502062,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/498162-second-edition-darklings?p=502046#post502046\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Um what?<br /> <br /> Any Durance where that gold digger has the oppotunity to talk to men would be an oppotunity.<br /> <br /> Heck, you're assuming that the Keeper chose her for her skills and choose a durance because of that. He might have chose her for her looks, or because she ate his food (he left it lying around on Earth by mistake). Her durance might be completely unrelated to her skills.<br /> <br /> Lets say that she ate some of his food and in return he sets her to work in the mines (my favourite example) she's working side by side with men, so she could seduce one and convince him to attack the guards - knowing that he'll die - so she can escape in the commotion.<br /> <br /> She wasn't abandoned, she wasn't loyal before or during her Durance. She's still a Darkling, intentionally getting someone killed is pretty Dark (and we now know it's certainly not Fairest).</div> </div> </div> </div>Not necessarily. <br /> <br /> For one, if she was chosen for beauty, the Keeper would turn her, in all likelihood... into a Statue. That cannot speak. Or countless other things... that cannot speak. There goes the primary opportunity. Especially as there are Gentry that like to punish, albeit not for good reasons, so could see doing this as, &quot;justice,&quot; for her, &quot;crimes,&quot; on Earth. <br /> <br /> Or a private lover that only is around the Keeper, with no access to other Changelings. Or, could be put into a role where there are no men, or only those who wouldn't care for her. The list goes on. <br /> <br /> I'm basing this off of that Gentry pick their Changelings based on something, and aren't just grabbing them at random. Why would a Keeper send her to the mines when that doesn't fit anything she was good or, for that matter, did in her prior life? <br /> <br /> I mean, I think you could make her work as a Darkling, but I feel like it'd be through betraying something that... doesn't primarily deal with using a skill set she already has, and already would have no qualms with using. And no, I do not buy that betraying something, even if it gets them killed, is that much of an extension for her. If anything, she may become a Beast because she's liberating herself from any of society's values, depending. <br /> <br /> <br /> To be fair, this may be over-reacting to chocolate in chocolate effect, so take my particular issues with a grain of salt if you wish. I kid, to some extent, but as I said, I see some of your point, I guess I just don't like the particular counter-examples, because in this case... it just comes off as me getting a chocolate ice cream cone, and dumping chocolate syrup all over it. But, that's not necessarily a bad thing I admit, so... <br /> <br /> Eh, your example seems to fit what we to some extent anyway. More of my argument now is that re-writing it to have more breadth I'd argue will weaken the writing because trying to broaden it would very possibly suck out its flavor. <br /> <br /> <br /> ON a side note, my issue with the Fairest was it being a single archetype, the leader, versus having a commonish origin(in this case Wasted Potential), because I found Wasted Potential was more than broad enough a theme for a Seeming. I just imagine that being any broader in background without it watering down the writing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1657-killer300","name":"Killer300","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"216"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-03T13:01:04-07:00","id":502064,"title":"","content":"I can't believe I didn't notice this post. Sorry Filamena.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Filamena</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/498162-second-edition-darklings?p=501331#post501331\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1)I was very careful to say 'many' and 'most' or ever 'some' in the text. I talked about trends not absolutes. Take a look, it's in there. I did plot out a specific skeleton for players to build their own flesh on to, but how many arms, legs, heads, all that stuff, that's on you. I also, because I'm talking about trends, want you to know that you don't have to use my skeleton in whole.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is what I disagree with though: That there is a trend.<br /> <br /> There's a million different ways to do &quot;what I needed to do&quot;. I don't think there should be any trend, or that you can accurately say &quot;most&quot; Changelings of a Seeming have backstory in common.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Filamena</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/498162-second-edition-darklings?p=501331#post501331\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why make it so specific instead of something more generic? Because I'm a professional writer and I want to tell stories with my work. If you don't want to use my story starters, you don't have to.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have to be blunt. This is a pretty awful answer.<br /> <br /> You're not even trying to argue that your write-up is what makes the best possible changeling book.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Filamena</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/498162-second-edition-darklings?p=501331#post501331\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">3)If you REALLY want me to make more generic material, my rate is 5 cents a word, half up front, half on turn over of the second draft. <img src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div> </div> </div> </div> The Background and Escape section for Darklings come up to 311 words. So $15.<br /> <br /> Was that a serious offer?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-03T13:03:33-07:00","id":502065,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/498162-second-edition-darklings?p=502064#post502064\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can't believe I didn't notice this post. Sorry Filamena.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> This is what I disagree with though: That there is a trend.<br /> <br /> There's a million different ways to do &quot;what I needed to do&quot;. I don't think there should be any trend, or that you can accurately say &quot;most&quot; Changelings of a Seeming have backstory in common.</div> </div> </div> </div>And this I'd argue, <br /> <br /> A. Is overestimating how narrow the origin of say, Loyalty is, seeing as you yourself crafted an example that still ended up involving on accident it seems, <br /> <br /> B. Ignores how the Gentry, and to some extent, Arcadia itself works. <br /> <br /> C. Is in danger of making it broad the point of being flavorless. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1657-killer300","name":"Killer300","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"216"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-03T13:11:11-07:00","id":502069,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Killer300</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/498162-second-edition-darklings?p=502065#post502065\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> C. Is in danger of making it broad the point of being flavorless.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Why? How is it that allowing numerous views on what it means to be betrayed (be it by people, circumstance, or your own sense of morals) flavorless? Isn't this entire medium about creativity by the player base?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5428-mr-feral","name":"Mr. Feral","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5428_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-03T13:16:07-07:00","id":502073,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Killer300</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/498162-second-edition-darklings?p=502062#post502062\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For one, if she was chosen for beauty, the Keeper would turn her, in all likelihood... into a Statue. Or a private lover that only is around the Keeper, with no access to other Changelings. Or, could be put into a role where there are no men, or only those who wouldn't care for her</div> </div> </div> </div> I disagree. Keepers are very very diverse. They might have all sorts of odd uses for a beautiful changeling.<br /> <br /> Also; these are fairy tales. When has locking a beautiful maiden in a tower <i>ever</i> kept the charming princes away?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Killer300</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/498162-second-edition-darklings?p=502062#post502062\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm basing this off of that Gentry pick their Changelings based on something, and aren't just grabbing them at random. Why would a Keeper send her to the mines when that doesn't fit anything she was good or, for that matter, did in her prior life?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sometimes keepers aren't picking randomly. Sometimes they are picking randomly. Other times they're not random but their logic is something utterly alien and makes no sense to humans.<br /> <br /> &quot;She's short and wears gold jewlrey. She's obviously miner material!&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Killer300</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/498162-second-edition-darklings?p=502062#post502062\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And no, I do not buy that betraying something, even if it gets them killed, is that much of an extension for her.</div> </div> </div> </div> Another disagreement.<br /> <br /> I cannot comprehend any argument where going form stealing money to intentionally getting someone killed is not &quot;that much of an extension&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Killer300</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/498162-second-edition-darklings?p=502062#post502062\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But, that's not necessarily a bad thing I admit, so...</div> </div> </div> </div> Exactly. It's a matter of taste. However splats need to support and encourage a broad verity of tastes.<br /> <br /> Flavour is important, but so is diversity. I'd point to the Vampire 2E Clans as a great example that hits that sweet spot. You can't tell me that they lack flavour, and they even have a list of examples which would provide a space for this current person who was loyal than to remain in the new version abandoned.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Killer300</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/498162-second-edition-darklings?p=502065#post502065\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A. Is overestimating how narrow the origin of say, Loyalty is, seeing as you yourself crafted an example that still ended up involving on accident it seems,</div> </div> </div> </div> I've come up with what, 4 or five examples by now in this thread? That criticism only applies to one of them - and it only half fits because Father Peter doesn't think God abandoned him, he thinks he abandoned God. Note that he remained faithful until the minuet he was offered a way out.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Killer300</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/498162-second-edition-darklings?p=502065#post502065\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">B. Ignores how the Gentry, and to some extent, Arcadia itself works.</div> </div> </div> </div> Please point to where in the books (outside these Seeming write ups) it says the Gentry and Arcadia work this way.<br /> <br /> And while you're doing that, please demonstrate why it would be bad to change that bit.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Killer300</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/498162-second-edition-darklings?p=502065#post502065\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">C. Is in danger of making it broad the point of being flavorless.</div> </div> </div> </div>Look at the 2E Clans for an example of what I'd like to see.<br /> <br /> Are the Clans flavourless?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 05-03-2015, 04:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-03T13:16:42-07:00","id":502076,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr. Feral</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/498162-second-edition-darklings?p=502069#post502069\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Why? How is it that allowing numerous views on what it means to be betrayed (be it by people, circumstance, or your own sense of morals) flavorless? Isn't this entire medium about creativity by the player base?</div> </div> </div> </div>Betrayal? That I think we already have a broad view on that. <br /> <br /> That, and the medium also needs good writing. <br /> <br /> Honestly though, the best compromise would probably be for the writers to just add two other examples that come from different perspectives in order to please everyone, while keeping good writing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1657-killer300","name":"Killer300","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"216"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-03T13:47:29-07:00","id":502130,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/498162-second-edition-darklings?p=502073#post502073\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I disagree. Keepers are very very diverse. They might have all sorts of odd uses for a beautiful changeling.<br /> <br /> Also; these are fairy tales. When has locking a beautiful maiden in a tower <i>ever</i> kept the charming princes away?</div> </div> </div> </div>When you're in a realm where a deity has virtually omnipotent control, it may cause a tad few difficulties.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Another disagreement.<br /> <br /> I cannot comprehend any argument where going form stealing money to intentionally getting someone killed is not &quot;that much of an extension&quot;. </div> </div> </div>Let me just drop this argument because, while I do have one, this gets into areas that don't concern the thread, and don't really matter to the over all discussion. <br /> <br /> So, I'm just going to concede this. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Exactly. It's a matter of taste. However splats need to support and encourage a broad verity of tastes.<br /> <br /> Flavour is important, but so is diversity. I'd point to the Vampire 2E Clans as a great example that hits that sweet spot. You can't tell me that they lack flavour, and they even have a list of examples which would provide a space for this current person who was loyal than to remain in the new version abandoned. </div> </div> </div>A. I just don't buy they need to be more broad, or at least, not in a way that changes current writing.. I think this issue could be solved with more examples, rather than trying to change the writing we already have. However Loyalty is an incredibly broad theme, and... your earlier example working just proves my point if your Golddigger still works under the current paradigm.<br /> <br /> B. Haven't read the clans, sorry. So... yeah, this argument is just lost on me. I do know Clans are mass social organizations, which I think makes them a tad bit different than Seemings, in how they're written and what they'll imply with it.<br /> <br /> C. That doesn't convince that broadening further, which I'd argue would result in destroying flavor, which is an unacceptable casualty in my view. There may be a of resolving this, but to me that would be adding further examples to writing we already have, rather than trying to to change the current writing to fit that goal.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Please point to where in the books (outside these Seeming write ups) it says the Gentry and Arcadia work this way. </div> </div> </div>From what I remember of Autumn Nightmares, the Gentry usually had some sort of goal with what they were kidnapping Changelings for. But, its been awhile, so let me concede this argument so we can just move on, okay? Just chalk up to me making a stupid argument. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Look at the 2E Clans for an example of what I'd like to see.<br /> <br /> Are the Clans flavourless? </div> </div> </div>For all we know, I would see the Clans as equally broad as the Seemings we currently have, as I haven't read the Clans.<br /> <br /> In case you're wondering, I've read Hunter, the original Changeling the Lost, some stuff connected to the Changeling the Lost and... the preview thread for Demon. That's about it, other than some bits and pieces here and there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1657,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1657-killer300","user":"Killer300","date":".  concessions 05-03-2015, 04:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1657-killer300","name":"Killer300","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"216"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-03T14:03:55-07:00","id":502150,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Killer300</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/498162-second-edition-darklings?p=502130#post502130\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When you're in a realm where a deity has virtually omnipotent control, it may cause a tad few difficulties.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>... Are you seriously saying a common faerie tale trope is inappropriate for Arcadia ?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Killer300</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/498162-second-edition-darklings?p=502130#post502130\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A. I just don't buy they need to be more broad, or at least, not in a way that changes current writing.. I think this issue could be solved with more examples</div> </div> </div> </div> If some of those more examples are about Darkspawn origins that don't involve loyalty than sure.<br /> <br /> The only reason why more examples alone wont work is that pesky word count limit.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Killer300</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/498162-second-edition-darklings?p=502130#post502130\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">your earlier example working just proves my point if your Golddigger still works under the current paradigm.</div> </div> </div> </div> No it doesn't, your argument was for Father Peter, not the gold digger.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Killer300</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/498162-second-edition-darklings?p=502130#post502130\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For all we know, I would see the Clans as equally broad as the Seemings we currently have, as I haven't read the Clans.</div> </div> </div> </div> Here's a breakdown of the Deeva write up.<br /> <br /> 3 paragraphs describing what the Clan are. This would be stuff like &quot;Fairest can't escape being leaders, people always look up to them and they fear letting them down&quot;.<br /> <br /> 4 different examples of a Deeva, each one paragraph long. If this was Darklings I'd put in one example of someone who was loyal and was abandoned here, and then use the other three for something different.<br /> <br /> Why you want to be us - one paragraph<br /> <br /> Why you should fear us - one paragraph<br /> <br /> Why we fear ourselves - one paragraph<br /> <br /> Clan Origins - about half a page of possible origins for the clan.<br /> <br /> Stereotypes.<br /> <br /> Charachter creation - half a page<br /> <br /> In the Covnanats - half a page.<br /> <br /> ------------------<br /> <br /> I'd like something similar for Seemings.<br /> <br /> A three paragraph overview.<br /> <br /> How we escaped - one paragraph.<br /> <br /> What holds us back - one paragraph<br /> <br /> How we move on - one paragraph<br /> <br /> Blessing<br /> <br /> Curse<br /> <br /> Character creation.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-03T14:14:24-07:00","id":502162,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/498162-second-edition-darklings?p=502150#post502150\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">... Are you seriously saying a common faerie tale trope is inappropriate for Arcadia ?</div> </div> </div> </div>I thought the simile meant sarcasm/joking...<br /> <br /> Okay, to be fair, colored text, but look, bad joke, move on.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If some of those more examples are about Darkspawn origins that don't involve loyalty than sure.<br /> <br /> The only reason why more examples alone wont work is that pesky word count limit. </div> </div> </div>Well, ouch. My only solution you liked is gone, especially as I really don't want to give up the current writing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> No it doesn't, your argument was for Father Peter, not the gold digger. </div> </div> </div>Ah, but the gold digger works under betrayal.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 4 different examples of a Deeva, each one paragraph long. If this was Darklings I'd put in one example of someone who was loyal and was abandoned here, and then use the other three for something different.<br /> <br /> Why you want to be us - one paragraph<br /> <br /> Why you should fear us - one paragraph<br /> <br /> Why we fear ourselves - one paragraph<br /> <br /> Clan Origins - about half a page of possible origins for the clan.<br /> <br /> Stereotypes.<br /> <br /> Charachter creation - half a page<br /> <br /> In the Covnanats - half a page. </div> </div> </div>Okay, all of this?<br /> <br /> Sounds like it had more words. Quite a few more actually.<br /> <br /> So really, this is an issue that either has to get solved by supplements or a larger word count. I fully admit the former isn't a good answer, and I'm not going to try to debate you on that, and the latter, well, you already gave the reason.<br /> <br /> I just like the current writing too much to want to see it get altered for it to be more broad. So... I guess we're at an impasse. Sorry.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1657-killer300","name":"Killer300","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"216"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-03T14:28:55-07:00","id":502178,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Killer300</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/498162-second-edition-darklings?p=502162#post502162\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ah, but the gold digger works under betrayal.</div> </div> </div> </div> Still doesn't work under the current paradigm.<br /> <br /> The current paradigm is:<br /> 1) A loyal person<br /> 2) Is abandoned<br /> 3) Betrays someone.<br /> <br /> The gold digger only has 1/3.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Killer300</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/498162-second-edition-darklings?p=502162#post502162\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sounds like it had more words. Quite a few more actually.</div> </div> </div> </div> It does, but I think the outline I proposed for Seemings could fit into the current word count.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Killer300</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/498162-second-edition-darklings?p=502162#post502162\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So... I guess we're at an impasse. Sorry.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. But I'm right <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-03T14:45:30-07:00","id":502187,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/498162-second-edition-darklings?p=502178#post502178\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It does, but I think the outline I proposed for Seemings could fit into the current word count.<br /> <br /> Yes. But I'm right <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>It might... <br /> <br /> But, it may not. I don't think its the best base to use seeing as the prior example had a higher word count to work with. To be fair, how much, I don't know, but still, its an interesting point. <br /> <br /> On a side note, I see what you guys want is just Betrayal as the base which... may work, but again, really don't want to change the current writing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1657-killer300","name":"Killer300","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"216"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-03T15:50:17-07:00","id":502244,"title":"","content":"What was wrong with the old Curse and Blessing? Nothing was wrong with them... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>nWoD Warhammer Fantasy RPG,<br /> WoD Wraith: The Oblivion<br /> and Infernum-style Demon: The Descent, Shadows of Abaddon --&gt; <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php/topic,26.0.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://madnessforums.com/forums/inde...opic,26.0.html</a><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","name":"MrParaduo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar974_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"967"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-03T15:59:47-07:00","id":502271,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrParaduo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/498162-second-edition-darklings?p=502244#post502244\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What was wrong with the old Curse and Blessing? Nothing was wrong with them... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>They have absolutely nothing to do with the new framework for Seeming Blessings and Curses, which offer opportunities for a free dot of Clarity and a breaking point for same once per story each.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-03T18:02:22-07:00","id":502344,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrParaduo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/498162-second-edition-darklings?p=502244#post502244\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What was wrong with the old Curse and Blessing? Nothing was wrong with them... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>What Satchel said. But additionally, please don't ascribe motivations. There doesn't have to be something &quot;wrong&quot; to do something that suits a different angle better.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-03T18:11:40-07:00","id":502352,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/498162-second-edition-darklings?p=502178#post502178\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It does, but I think the outline I proposed for Seemings could fit into the current word count.<br /> <br /> Yes. But I'm right <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>FWIW, my personal policy is to never ask for more than a rewrite of 20% of content, unless a writer didn't listen to my direction at all. What functionally amounts to &quot;just do it all over in a different format&quot; isn't likely to happen. It's not fair to the talent, in my opinion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-03T18:22:21-07:00","id":502357,"title":"","content":"As long as it has sufficient breadth, I think it will be fine.<br /> <br /> It does feel too narrow as it is and while a strict reading is fine, it'd be nice to not make it easy to fall into the 1E stereotype trap of &quot;All X are Y&quot; sort of mould.<br /> <br /> I do really like the core idea, though!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1462-xenesis","name":"Xenesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1462_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-03T18:31:30-07:00","id":502364,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/498162-second-edition-darklings?p=498215#post498215\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'll clarify in the later draft. The point is, blindly following is the problem. Not having a Plan B. Not paying attention to exits. Putting your safety solely in someone else's hands. Fundamental, deep trust.</div> </div> </div> </div>I know someone like this: he's exceedingly self-reliant, is a big believer in hard choices, and doesn't trust anyone further than he can throw them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-03T21:40:08-07:00","id":502477,"title":"","content":"King's Raven, you seem to have a problem with the idea that characters with a given Seeming can have commonalities of any sort, to the point that you've said or at least very strongly implied that any commonality beyond &quot;did what I had to&quot; is bad and constraining and limiting and very close to morally wrong. Yet &quot;did what I had to&quot; is itself a constraint, and you've stated that any sort of constraint is unendurable. Frankly, you seem to have the causality reversed: Seemings do not cause changelings possessing them to have traits in common. It is the sharing of traits that results in shared Seemings. To use a fairly close analogy, think of fire fighters. All firefighters have certain personality traits in common, such as physical courage and a drive to help people in need, because those who lack the traits <i>\u200bdo not become firefighters</i>. Being a firefighter does not cause a person to have those traits; having those traits leads them to become firefighters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1184,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","user":"LadyLens","date":". 05-04-2015, 12:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-03T23:27:04-07:00","id":502553,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/498162-second-edition-darklings?p=502352#post502352\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">FWIW, my personal policy is to never ask for more than a rewrite of 20% of content, unless a writer didn't listen to my direction at all. What functionally amounts to &quot;just do it all over in a different format&quot; isn't likely to happen. It's not fair to the talent, in my opinion.</div> </div> </div> </div> Sounds like a whole different world, I'm used to to Princess development where we're utterly ruthless about rewriting stuff.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LadyLens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/498162-second-edition-darklings?p=502477#post502477\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">King's Raven, you seem to have a problem with the idea that characters with a given Seeming can have commonalities of any sort, to the point that you've said or at least very strongly implied that any commonality beyond &quot;did what I had to&quot; is bad and constraining and limiting and very close to morally wrong.</div> </div> </div> </div> &quot;Morally wrong&quot;???<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LadyLens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/498162-second-edition-darklings?p=502477#post502477\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yet &quot;did what I had to&quot; is itself a constraint, and you've stated that any sort of constraint is unendurable.</div> </div> </div> </div>Firstly you yourself said I complained about constraints <i>beyond </i>that - so there's no logical paradox.<br /> <br /> Secondly that's not actually my viewpoint.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LadyLens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/498162-second-edition-darklings?p=502477#post502477\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It is the sharing of traits that results in shared Seemings. To use a fairly close analogy, think of fire fighters. All firefighters have certain personality traits in common, such as physical courage and a drive to help people in need, because those who lack the traits <i>\u200bdo not become firefighters</i>. Being a firefighter does not cause a person to have those traits; having those traits leads them to become firefighters.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's sort of what I think.<br /> <br /> I think that any person can become any Seeming, but certian personality traits make others more likely. Even the nicest person is going to be tempted to betray someone and become a Darkling if they thoght it would help them escape because Arcadia is just that bad. But a more trecherous person is more likely to think in that direction.<br /> <br /> But the current write up is saying &quot;you became a firefighter because you were burnt when you were younger&quot; and encourages you to write about how you got burnt. That's too narrow I'd prefer a write up that talks directly about the traits that leads to a Darkling and encourages players to be creative with their backstory.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-03T23:45:45-07:00","id":502559,"title":"","content":"Well the current write-ups on reading them all are stating a common way these Seemings end up in Arcadia... This isn't just for Darklings, it's for Beasts and Fairest too. They all seem to point in different ways how the mortal ran away from the world and the Keeper welcomed them into Arcadia... Beasts dream of a world outside their deadend life and escapism, Fairest realise their lives have been wasted and decide to run away... It seems a common theme of getting to Arcadia is running away or wanting to do so, from your former life. The Seeming also seems linked to a reinforcement of the event that brought your character into Arcadia... Beasts forego their former doormat status to tear free from their cages a second time, Darklings betrayed twice lose their faith in trust and Fairest realise in a missed potential that needs freeing, the second time in others around them.<br /> <br /> I see that a betrayal seems to be the main and most prevalant lead-in to Arcadia from a Darkling pov, though a changeling could easily form into either a Beast or Fairest in reaction to their deadend stifled life of missed chances, depending on personal choice. The Darkling could just feel betrayed rather than actively be it before they leave for Arcadia on realisation or coming across one of these missed chances in life where they could have achieved something better but are stuck unmoving and static still.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3951-wander","name":"wander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"409"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-03T23:54:36-07:00","id":502563,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/498162-second-edition-darklings?p=502553#post502553\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Sounds like a whole different world, I'm used to to Princess development where we're utterly ruthless about rewriting stuff.</div> </div> </div> </div>Starkly different. I'm hiring people that are working for paychecks, and on deadlines. Every word they have to rewrite is a word they aren't getting paid additionally for, and more time taken out of other contracts. I have had editing notes that turned my normal 10 hour work day into a 16 hour work day for two weeks. I won't do that to other writers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-04T02:36:33-07:00","id":502663,"title":"","content":"It's hard for me to get my head around that way of working. I'm constantly going back to stuff I worked on and changing it if I have a better idea. I suppose the fact I'm a software developer might also have something to do with it; even the idea that something is done and thus you can't or shouldn't go back and change it is alien to our industry.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-04T05:11:11-07:00","id":502785,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/498162-second-edition-darklings?p=502352#post502352\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> FWIW, my personal policy is to never ask for more than a rewrite of 20% of content, unless a writer didn't listen to my direction at all. What functionally amounts to &quot;just do it all over in a different format&quot; isn't likely to happen. It's not fair to the talent, in my opinion.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, I sincerely hope that I am phrasing this so that it is not misconstrued. I do not want this to sound accusatory or indignant, and if it does it is not my intention. I genuinely want to know what, to you, is the purpose of putting these notes up. I don't want my comments to be entirely pointless if they contravene any idea of what might be done with them. As it stands, I and others see issues that we feel need to be addressed, not for our personal enjoyment, but so this series we have devoted so much time to can live up to its own potential. As I see it, there are areas to improve. That takes tweaking and in some cases reworking what has been written which, to me, is the purpose of the writer and the goal of putting things up for comment.<br /> <br /> I am aware that there are people who are happy with this, but they would have been satisfied anyway. If this is meant as a teaser to those fans and nothing more, I understand.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5428-mr-feral","name":"Mr. Feral","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5428_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-04T08:14:59-07:00","id":502931,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/498162-second-edition-darklings?p=502663#post502663\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's hard for me to get my head around that way of working. I'm constantly going back to stuff I worked on and changing it if I have a better idea. I suppose the fact I'm a software developer might also have something to do with it; even the idea that something is done and thus you can't or shouldn't go back and change it is alien to our industry.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the limitations do a lot to bring out the best. Heaven forbid I'd probably be published with my novels already if I adopted a 1.5 shot with them, and I'd focus a lot more on getting it right rather than constantly painting over it again and again.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-04T08:25:25-07:00","id":502937,"title":"","content":"Well... that got settled.<br /> <br /> But yeah, going to have to wait for supplements, if say, we wanted to have more official, if you will, stuff on Darklings, as I'm assuming expanded wordcount is out.<br /> <br /> Also, ArcaneArts does have a point. Creative writing isn't like software development. Yes, editing is important, but it can prevent a work from being completed at all.<br /> <br /> As for Princess... that's open-source. That, and there's no release date, if you will, so essentially, it can be perfected with no real negative real world consequences. That... isn't the case here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1657-killer300","name":"Killer300","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"216"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-04T08:38:54-07:00","id":502966,"title":"","content":"There's some consequences. The first draft tends to be the sharpest and brightest stuff a writer will put out because it's just raw word work. Edit it it too much and it's super easy to lose edge and vividness.<br /> <br /> Editing and polish is like makeup-you do enough to bring out the best of what's there, not so much as to cake over it.<br /> <br /> The amount of time driven-by-committee, big-fan-projects have is both their joy and failing. Enough critique to pass as pro, processed enough to be dead.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-04T08:47:31-07:00","id":502973,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr. Feral</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/498162-second-edition-darklings?p=502785#post502785\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Okay, I sincerely hope that I am phrasing this so that it is not misconstrued. I do not want this to sound accusatory or indignant, and if it does it is not my intention. I genuinely want to know what, to you, is the purpose of putting these notes up. I don't want my comments to be entirely pointless if they contravene any idea of what might be done with them. As it stands, I and others see issues that we feel need to be addressed, not for our personal enjoyment, but so this series we have devoted so much time to can live up to its own potential. As I see it, there are areas to improve. That takes tweaking and in some cases reworking what has been written which, to me, is the purpose of the writer and the goal of putting things up for comment.<br /> <br /> I am aware that there are people who are happy with this, but they would have been satisfied anyway. If this is meant as a teaser to those fans and nothing more, I understand.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well it's not that there's no room for critique. They're just not going to totally re-write it. Up to 20%, from what Dave said, could be re-written, they're just not going to scrap half the writeup and do it again.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-04T08:53:03-07:00","id":502982,"title":"","content":"I've been shown some of the earlier drafts for a few books(like Flowers of Hell and such). Not every developer necessarily plays by David's rules, of course, but believe me when I say they do listen to feedback.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-04T09:17:15-07:00","id":502992,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr. Feral</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/498162-second-edition-darklings?p=502785#post502785\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Okay, I sincerely hope that I am phrasing this so that it is not misconstrued. I do not want this to sound accusatory or indignant, and if it does it is not my intention. I genuinely want to know what, to you, is the purpose of putting these notes up. I don't want my comments to be entirely pointless if they contravene any idea of what might be done with them. As it stands, I and others see issues that we feel need to be addressed, not for our personal enjoyment, but so this series we have devoted so much time to can live up to its own potential. As I see it, there are areas to improve. That takes tweaking and in some cases reworking what has been written which, to me, is the purpose of the writer and the goal of putting things up for comment.<br /> <br /> I am aware that there are people who are happy with this, but they would have been satisfied anyway. If this is meant as a teaser to those fans and nothing more, I understand.</div> </div> </div> </div>I probably put more effort out than any other single developer to be open, to discuss, to share, and to revise in accordance to feedback I find valuable. Every bit of material I put up in first draft form, I expect to put through revision work, and often that means with much of that input in mind. Anyone that was present for the Blood &amp; Smoke open development should be able to attest. <br /> <br /> I'm too far along to send things back to the drawing board, but I do make plenty of adjustments. You'd be shocked how much 20% can mean. But I'm not going to make an author do twice the work for the same pay to accommodate the specific pitches of a person on a forum. I hope that doesn't sound completely off-base and unfair. If it does, I'm sorry. It's not something I'm interested in compromising on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-04T09:42:48-07:00","id":503019,"title":"","content":"The character description of Darklings feels more like just the Antiquarian kith than the Seeming as a whole. Weren't Darklings meant to be centered around fear and trickery?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>nWoD Warhammer Fantasy RPG,<br /> WoD Wraith: The Oblivion<br /> and Infernum-style Demon: The Descent, Shadows of Abaddon --&gt; <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php/topic,26.0.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://madnessforums.com/forums/inde...opic,26.0.html</a><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","name":"MrParaduo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar974_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"967"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-04T10:13:39-07:00","id":503046,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrParaduo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/498162-second-edition-darklings?p=503019#post503019\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The character description of Darklings feels more like just the Antiquarian kith than the Seeming as a whole. Weren't Darklings meant to be centered around fear and trickery?</div> </div> </div> </div>New edition, new themes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-04T10:28:51-07:00","id":503055,"title":"","content":"I .... don't seem to get what the arguing over here is. Starting at page 9 and going forwards, I'm confused at what's going on here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-04T10:36:15-07:00","id":503067,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/498162-second-edition-darklings?p=502992#post502992\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm not going to make an author do twice the work for the same pay to accommodate the specific pitches of a person on a forum..</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think that is unfair, especially given how contentious the internet is known to be. I also don't see the need for a 100% rewrite of this (although it's not entirely inconceivable that such a thing could happen). Really all these mentions of &quot;most&quot; or &quot;some&quot; fall flat because the writeup does not explain what the other options are outside of that and is written in such a way that it seems to genuinely discourage other attempts to move within the framework. This could be amended with a few more examples or some slightly more general phrasing. Not, as has been suggested, a dumbing down and making generic the entire work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5428-mr-feral","name":"Mr. Feral","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5428_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-04T10:55:30-07:00","id":503103,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr. Feral</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/498162-second-edition-darklings?p=503067#post503067\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't think that is unfair, especially given how contentious the internet is known to be. I also don't see the need for a 100% rewrite of this (although it's not entirely inconceivable that such a thing could happen). Really all these mentions of &quot;most&quot; or &quot;some&quot; fall flat because the writeup does not explain what the other options are outside of that and is written in such a way that it seems to genuinely discourage other attempts to move within the framework. This could be amended with a few more examples or some slightly more general phrasing. Not, as has been suggested, a dumbing down and making generic the entire work.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would not object to slightly more generalized phrasing, and more examples are always good, if there's wordcount available for them. I don't personally see how it discourages movement within the framework, but that seems to be a common enough sentiment, I assume it's me who's not seeing it. Could you point out an example of where or how it does this?<br /> <br /> To me, it reads like a description of a general trend: people like this often end up in these kinds of situations in Arcadia, which tends to lead to this stuff happening, and they have to do something like this to escape. Afterwards, they can regain Clarity by doing this for these reasons, but this other thing is a breaking point for these other reasons. Treat it as a general tendency, and decide in what ways your character is an exception to these trends, and in what ways he or she follows them.<br /> <br /> King's Raven has said that he doesn't want there to be any trends, so I don't think it's going to possible for both of us to be satisfied. Different expressions of the trend are great. Exceptions to the trend are wonderful. Not even having a trend? It would lose what makes it powerful to me in the process.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-04T11:06:30-07:00","id":503115,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/498162-second-edition-darklings?p=503055#post503055\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I .... don't seem to get what the arguing over here is. Starting at page 9 and going forwards, I'm confused at what's going on here.</div> </div> </div> </div>There are like at least three different arguments going on at once between the same five or six people, I don't blame you for not being able to follow it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-04T11:44:04-07:00","id":503199,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/498162-second-edition-darklings?p=503103#post503103\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">King's Raven has said that he doesn't want there to be any trends, so I don't think it's going to possible for both of us to be satisfied. Different expressions of the trend are great. Exceptions to the trend are wonderful. Not even having a trend? It would lose what makes it powerful to me in the process.</div> </div> </div> </div>And that's something I don't understand.<br /> <br /> What's powerful to you is this particular story - the story of someone who was taken advantage of and resolved to loose the positive traits that made them a target.<br /> <br /> I get that, but what I don't understand is why that story looses something if you change it from a general trend to a specific example? The vampire clan write ups have a set of examples, what would this loose if the loyal guy became one of them?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-04T11:59:49-07:00","id":503231,"title":"","content":"Well, in any case, I just want to say that, despite the issues I have with the Fairest, I really like the Beast and Darkling write ups. I think they're pretty awesome, and I would like to extend my appreciation for a job well done to the writer! Thank you for the good work!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-04T12:04:38-07:00","id":503234,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/498162-second-edition-darklings?p=503199#post503199\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And that's something I don't understand.<br /> <br /> What's powerful to you is this particular story - the story of someone who was taken advantage of and resolved to loose the positive traits that made them a target.<br /> <br /> I get that, but what I don't understand is why that story looses something if you change it from a general trend to a specific example? The vampire clan write ups have a set of examples, what would this loose if the loyal guy became one of them?</div> </div> </div> </div>It just changes what the Seeming represents. It stops being an X-splat of survivors of a particular kind of abuse and becomes... I don't even know, people who made a dick move one time to get out of Arcadia? The individual story doesn't lose its power to me, but the Splat as a whole loses its identity. I don't want to speak for other people, but I think that's what Onega and Killer are getting at when they say it would make it dull and generic. I wouldn't put it quite that way because I think it's unnecessarily hyperbolic. But I do agree with the core sentiment that the Seeming would be less compelling if it was just a group of &quot;spooky changelings&quot; or &quot;jerky changelings&quot; or whatever, instead of being a shared identity between survivors who cope with their trauma in similar ways.<br /> <br /> Again, doesn't mean there shouldn't be exceptions, or that those exceptions shouldn't get a fair treatment in the writeup. I just want Seeming to have more meaning than a simple category.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 05-04-2015, 03:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-04T12:10:54-07:00","id":503240,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/498162-second-edition-darklings?p=503234#post503234\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It just changes what the Seeming represents. It stops being an X-splat of survivors of a particular kind of abuse and becomes... I don't even know, people who made a dick move one time to get out of Arcadia? The individual story doesn't lose its power to me, but the Splat as a whole loses its identity. I don't want to speak for other people, but I think that's what Onega and Killer are getting at when they say it would make it dull and generic. I wouldn't put it quite that way because I think it's unnecessarily hyperbolic. But I do agree with the core sentiment that the Seeming would be less compelling if it was just a group of &quot;spooky changelings&quot; or &quot;jerky changelings&quot; or whatever, instead of being a shared identity between survivors who cope with their trauma in similar ways.<br /> <br /> Again, doesn't mean there shouldn't be exceptions, or that those exceptions shouldn't get a fair treatment in the writeup. I just want Seeming to have more meaning than a simple category.</div> </div> </div> </div>Its that, and also that... I liked the writing so much that I really didn't want to see it modified too much. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1657-killer300","name":"Killer300","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"216"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-04T12:30:37-07:00","id":503255,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/498162-second-edition-darklings?p=503234#post503234\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It just changes what the Seeming represents. It stops being an X-splat of survivors of a particular kind of abuse and becomes... I don't even know, people who made a dick move one time to get out of Arcadia? The individual story doesn't lose its power to me, but the Splat as a whole loses its identity. I don't want to speak for other people, but I think that's what Onega and Killer are getting at when they say it would make it dull and generic. I wouldn't put it quite that way because I think it's unnecessarily hyperbolic. But I do agree with the core sentiment that the Seeming would be less compelling if it was just a group of &quot;spooky changelings&quot; or &quot;jerky changelings&quot; or whatever, instead of being a shared identity between survivors who cope with their trauma in similar ways.<br /> <br /> Again, doesn't mean there shouldn't be exceptions, or that those exceptions shouldn't get a fair treatment in the writeup. I just want Seeming to have more meaning than a simple category.</div> </div> </div> </div>Now I understand.<br /> <br /> I kind of agree that a Seeming is &quot;a shared identity between survivors who cope with their trauma in similar ways&quot;, though I see that as subordiante to a Seeming being the way you regained your freedom.<br /> <br /> However to me the problem is that the current write up is:<br /> <br /> &quot;a shared identity between survivors who <u>mostly suffered similar abuses and</u> cope with their trauma in similar ways&quot;<br /> <br /> When it should be<br /> <br /> &quot;a shared identity between survivors who <u>each suffered different abuses but</u> cope with their trauma in similar ways&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> In the real world there might be strong correlations between how you were abused and the coping mechanisms you develop; but I think that in Arcadia there shouldn't be - because roleplaying games should encourage creative charachters.<br /> <br /> <br /> If I may be so bold; I think, Charlaquin, what you want from a Seeming would be better suited as an Entitlement (if they're still in 2E?). Look at the Duchy of the Icebound Heart from the 1E corebook. That's a great example of &quot;a shared identity between survivors who cope with their trauma in similar ways&quot;.<br /> <br /> If the Darkling Seeming was broader and there was an Entitlement for this specific concept; then we can both have our cake and eat it. (You know, in the world where you can rewrite these things)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-04T12:41:47-07:00","id":503268,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/498162-second-edition-darklings?p=503255#post503255\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> However to me the problem is that the current write up is:<br /> <br /> &quot;a shared identity between survivors who <u>mostly suffered similar abuses and</u> cope with their trauma in similar ways&quot;<br /> <br /> When it should be<br /> <br /> &quot;a shared identity between survivors who <u>each suffered different abuses but</u> cope with their trauma in similar ways&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>The latter is a freehold. The latter is changeling community in general.<br /> <br /> The former is the little group of guys who go to the local Sonic after the meetings, share some drinks and hot dogs, and talk about the particulars no one else seems to gets.<br /> <br /> EDIT: This stands true of even first edition: THe Fairest commiserated with each other because they suffered pleasures unfathomable to the others and had to rise above the sensation. Ogres could drink together when they couldn't for any other reason because of their involvement with violence. Darklings would give each other the nod of recognition for knowing that each other had to fumble through the dark paths.<br /> <br /> It's just clearer now just what exactly those shared experiences are. They share not only choices, but places where they got hurt the most, and commiserate how these likenesses led them to where they felt they had to go.<br /> <br /> I'm not a hundred percent sold on the story structure built in, BUT! The narrative provided is interesting enough with plenty of hooks to challenge, reinterpret, deconstruct, subvert, and such that I'm willing to play around with it for a bit before I go in and rewrite things.<br /> <br /> So, like, 85 to 90% sold.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 05-04-2015, 03:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-04T12:58:01-07:00","id":503282,"title":"","content":"The thing about the Seeming writeups to me is that all of them begin with what the changeling-to-be was like <i>before</i> her Durance. The seed of who or what the changeling became was there all along, albeit in the negative. The Fairest was too passive, shirking her responsibilities; the Darkling was too trusting and had too many lines she wouldn't cross.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-04T13:12:31-07:00","id":503293,"title":"","content":"Stories of hard lessons, what?<br /> <br /> As a game of saving yourself, it makes sense that changelings would have traits that held them back. As a game of the cruelty of narrative and dream logic, it makes sense that similar issues get faced with similar trials and produce similar results. There is <i>some</i> structure to the Wyrd, after all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-04T14:16:13-07:00","id":503484,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Killer300</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/498162-second-edition-darklings?p=503240#post503240\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Its that, and also that... I liked the writing so much that I really didn't want to see it modified too much.</div> </div> </div> </div>Gotcha. I'm not too worried about that myself, because I know Filamena is an excellent writer and I trust that what ever revisions she makes will be just as well-written as this draft, if not better.<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/498162-second-edition-darklings?p=503255#post503255\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now I understand.<br /> <br /> I kind of agree that a Seeming is &quot;a shared identity between survivors who cope with their trauma in similar ways&quot;, though I see that as subordiante to a Seeming being the way you regained your freedom.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree with you on that. I think there's a lot of room for variations on the backgrounds that Darklings might come from, the kinds of challenges they may have faced in their Durance, even the particulars of their escape, but the single most defining feature is definitely how they reclaimed agency. That's why I think all of your examples work fine as Darklings, because they escaped via some kind of betrayal. I still see their backgrounds as atypical for Darklings, but there's nothing wrong with that. Player characters in RPGs are almost always exceptional people (with a few exceptions where being average is an important part of the themes), so there's absolutely nothing wrong with creating a character who is an exception to the &quot;usual&quot; background.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/498162-second-edition-darklings?p=503255#post503255\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">However to me the problem is that the current write up is:<br /> <br /> &quot;a shared identity between survivors who <u>mostly suffered similar abuses and</u> cope with their trauma in similar ways&quot;<br /> <br /> When it should be<br /> <br /> &quot;a shared identity between survivors who <u>each suffered different abuses but</u> cope with their trauma in similar ways&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>The former is probably a better description of what I'd like Seeming to represent, with the caveat that they don't <i>necessarily</i> have to have suffered similar abuses, it's just that they often did, because abusers tend to go after similar kinds of victims, and those victims often have similar coping mechanisms (but not always).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/498162-second-edition-darklings?p=503255#post503255\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the real world there might be strong correlations between how you were abused and the coping mechanisms you develop; but I think that in Arcadia there shouldn't be - because roleplaying games should encourage creative charachters.</div> </div> </div> </div>Personally, I think the current writeup does encourage creative characters. Restrictions breed creativity.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/498162-second-edition-darklings?p=503255#post503255\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I may be so bold; I think, Charlaquin, what you want from a Seeming would be better suited as an Entitlement (if they're still in 2E?). Look at the Duchy of the Icebound Heart from the 1E corebook. That's a great example of &quot;a shared identity between survivors who cope with their trauma in similar ways&quot;.<br /> <br /> If the Darkling Seeming was broader and there was an Entitlement for this specific concept; then we can both have our cake and eat it. (You know, in the world where you can rewrite these things)</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that <i>could </i>work, but I'm with Arcane on this being more what I see Seeming covering, whereas Entitlements would share a more specific expression of the general trend that the Seeming covers.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/498162-second-edition-darklings?p=503282#post503282\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The thing about the Seeming writeups to me is that all of them begin with what the changeling-to-be was like <i>before</i> her Durance. The seed of who or what the changeling became was there all along, albeit in the negative. The Fairest was too passive, shirking her responsibilities; the Darkling was too trusting and had too many lines she wouldn't cross.</div> </div> </div> </div>This was kind of the case in 1e as well. 1e Fairest were taken because they had a beauty or talent that their Keeper coveted and wished to possess. 1e Darklings were taken as punishment for some offense or transgression that they (often unwittingly) committed against their Keeper. Beasts were taken because they couldn't resist the call of the wild and were lured right into their Keeper's domain. Background has always been a part of Kith, it's just that now it ties into the abuse metaphor more appropriately.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-04T14:32:51-07:00","id":503496,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/498162-second-edition-darklings?p=503484#post503484\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Player characters in RPGs are almost always exceptional people (with a few exceptions where being average is an important part of the themes), so there's absolutely nothing wrong with creating a character who is an exception to the &quot;usual&quot; background.</div> </div> </div> </div> It's not just about the PCs. It's about the NPCs. You're going to have a lot of NPC changelings so you want them to all be different, it's far more interesting that way.<br /> <br /> P.S. Not all my examples escaped via betrayal. We've been through this before. Bob Average never knew the guy he killed. But murder still makes a Darkling.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/498162-second-edition-darklings?p=503484#post503484\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The former is probably a better description of what I'd like Seeming to represent, with the caveat that they don't <i>necessarily</i> have to have suffered similar abuses, it's just that they often did, because abusers tend to go after similar kinds of victims, and those victims often have similar coping mechanisms (but not always).</div> </div> </div> </div> I think you're thinking of the Gentry too much like humans. The gentry have reasons, but often ones that make no sense from a human perspective. There's only so much an understadning of human abuse dynamics can do when you're thinking about the guy who got turned into a painting or a pillar of fire.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/498162-second-edition-darklings?p=503484#post503484\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally, I think the current writeup does encourage creative characters. Restrictions breed creativity.</div> </div> </div> </div> That's true, but there's more than one kind of creativity.<br /> <br /> Perhaps I should have used the word &quot;diversity&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/498162-second-edition-darklings?p=503484#post503484\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that <i>could </i>work, but I'm with Arcane on this being more what I see Seeming covering, whereas Entitlements would share a more specific expression of the general trend that the Seeming covers.</div> </div> </div> </div> I agree with that, but the Seeming as Filamena wrote it is already very specific. if you overlook qualifiers like most.<br /> <br /> If Darklings are everyone who escaped by &quot;doing what I had to do&quot; then you can easily think of more specific expressions. Starting with the write up about loyalty. <br /> <br /> I can't think of any more specific expressions you could base an Entitlement around for the loyalty guy.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/498162-second-edition-darklings?p=503484#post503484\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This was kind of the case in 1e as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, but 1E seemings were different things so it worked there.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-04T14:47:59-07:00","id":503509,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/498162-second-edition-darklings?p=503496#post503496\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> It's not just about the PCs. It's about the NPCs. You're going to have a lot of NPC changelings so you want them to all be different, it's far more interesting that way.<br /> <br /> P.S. Not all my examples escaped via betrayal. We've been through this before. Bob Average never knew the guy he killed. But murder still makes a Darkling.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, sorry, betrayal was a poor choice of words on my part. Via doing what must be done at any cost, I guess.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/498162-second-edition-darklings?p=503496#post503496\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think you're thinking of the Gentry too much like humans. The gentry have reasons, but often ones that make no sense from a human perspective. There's only so much an understadning of human abuse dynamics can do when you're thinking about the guy who got turned into a painting or a pillar of fire.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think this comes down to taste, I find the Gentry more compelling as a living embodiment of narrative than as unknowable eldritch horrors, and since most writers are human, most narratives cover human drama, ergo the Gentry pretty much embody human drama to me.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/498162-second-edition-darklings?p=503496#post503496\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's true, but there's more than one kind of creativity.<br /> <br /> Perhaps I should have used the word &quot;diversity&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair enough. I don't think this writeup <i>discourages</i> diversity of characters, but I have no objection to revising it to be a bit more <i>encouraging</i> of it. Personally, I think more examples and some more open wording should be sufficient to accomplish that, but evidently you don't agree.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/498162-second-edition-darklings?p=503496#post503496\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I agree with that, but the Seeming as Filamena wrote it is already very specific. if you overlook qualifiers like most.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why would you do that? Those qualifiers are written into the text. If you're going to intentionally overlook parts of the text, don't criticize it for the absence of those parts. They're there, stop overlooking them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/498162-second-edition-darklings?p=503496#post503496\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If Darklings are everyone who escaped by &quot;doing what I had to do&quot; then you can easily think of more specific expressions. Starting with the write up about loyalty.<br /> <br /> I can't think of any more specific expressions you could base an Entitlement around for the loyalty guy.</div> </div> </div> </div>The loyalty guy is one guy. Yes, lots of Darklings had similar experiences to that guy. No, those people are not the only people who are allowed to be Darklings.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/498162-second-edition-darklings?p=503496#post503496\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sure, but 1E seemings were different things so it worked there.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm... That's really interesting that you say that, because I didn't think it worked <i>at all</i> in 1e. It's starting to become clear that you and I just like totally different things in Changeling.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-04T15:05:19-07:00","id":503530,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/498162-second-edition-darklings?p=503509#post503509\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think this comes down to taste, I find the Gentry more compelling as a living embodiment of narrative than as unknowable eldritch horrors, and since most writers are human, most narratives cover human drama, ergo the Gentry pretty much embody human drama to me.</div> </div> </div> </div> Living embodyment of narrative, sure.<br /> <br /> But even when we're talking about human drama. Anyone can talk to an abuse victim, because an abuse victim is another human. But the abuse victim's life story, if it got up and started walking.<br /> <br /> Sure you can understand the life story, you can look at the individual charchters and understand them as people. You can look at the events and understand them. You can even understand how it all fits togeather.<br /> <br /> But how do you have a <i>conversation</i> with that life story? What does the life story <i>want</i>? What would <i>offend</i> it? Trying to relate to someone's life story, or any story, like it was a person isn't as far out there as interacting with an Abyssal Intruder. But it's close.<br /> <br /> <br /> So - if you're abducted and abused, or abducted and enslaved, by a story. I wouldn't expect the dynamic to resemble human - human abuse.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/498162-second-edition-darklings?p=503509#post503509\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fair enough. I don't think this writeup <i>discourages</i> diversity of characters, but I have no objection to revising it to be a bit more <i>encouraging</i> of it. Personally, I think more examples and some more open wording should be sufficient to accomplish that, but evidently you don't agree.</div> </div> </div> </div> No that's what I've been saying all along.<br /> <br /> The thing is; to me encouraging would require several options being given equal weight. Either you'd have two more Background and Escape sections for each Seeming at a large wordcount epansion; or you would need to redesign the entire layout to fit several examples in the same wordcount. Which is why I've been suggesting a different layout.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/498162-second-edition-darklings?p=503509#post503509\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why would you do that? Those qualifiers are written into the text.</div> </div> </div> </div> That's a fair question - why would I do that?<br /> <br /> Because like you say, &quot;it doesn't discourage it, but it doesn't encourage it either&quot;. I overlook the qualifiers, because the impression it gives to me is the impression you'd get sans qualifiers.<br /> <br /> Heck; the word &quot;most&quot; is an anti-qualifier. It says they're exceptions but theose exceptions are rare. I might go so far to say the use of the word &quot;most&quot; is explicitly discouraging diversity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-04T16:23:24-07:00","id":503600,"title":"","content":"I think there needs to be reason behind the Seemings and as such, having something that qualifies that person to gain it needs to be in place. Otherwise it becomes down to random luck what a character is and I'd like to think more narrative credit in what I create as my characters than 'this guy just happens to be a XX because... umm... I liked the benefits they get'. This type of arguing already has had the writer chime-in and now they're even rewriting the Seeming... This kind of thing just means the book may end up being delayed and just because a <i>few sentences</i> weren't worded in a <i>very specific way</i> to how three people took umbrage with...<br /> <br /> <i>C'mon gang</i>. It's a first draft, let's not make dissertations over two words changing the tone of a general paragraph.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3951-wander","name":"wander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"409"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-04T16:33:51-07:00","id":503606,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/498162-second-edition-darklings?p=503600#post503600\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think there needs to be reason behind the Seemings and as such, having something that qualifies that person to gain it needs to be in place. Otherwise it becomes down to random luck what a character is and I'd like to think more narrative credit in what I create as my characters than 'this guy just happens to be a XX because... umm... I liked the benefits they get'. This type of arguing already has had the writer chime-in and now they're even rewriting the Seeming... This kind of thing just means the book may end up being delayed and just because a <i>few sentences</i> weren't worded in a <i>very specific way</i> to how three people took umbrage with...</div> </div> </div> </div>Err... They're not re-writing it... There may be some changes between this draft and the next one, but Dave did kind of specifically say he doesn't ask writers on books he develops for to change more than 20% from the first draft unless it's way off-base.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/498162-second-edition-darklings?p=503600#post503600\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>C'mon gang</i>. It's a first draft, let's not make dissertations over two words changing the tone of a general paragraph.</div> </div> </div> </div>Let's be fair to the people who are offering critique. It's not about a few words or the tone. It's about whether or not the current writeup leaves enough room for characters of various backgrounds and who experienced different Durances.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 05-04-2015, 07:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-04T16:42:16-07:00","id":503613,"title":"","content":"To share my view of the Gentry, which I probably should've stated a bit back, I view them as psychopathic children who never grew up. They're selfish, incapable of empathizing with those they hurt, or worse choose not to, and do everything for fun. <br /> <br /> Obviously, this is just one interpretation, but, its the lens by which I view the Gentry. Less Eldritch Abomination, more the child tearing off a spider's legs for the fun of it. The spoiled child that never learned to respect other people as more than objects to gain pleasure from. Them lacking creativity fits into this, which I note is emphasized, because they need other persons to give them entertainment. <br /> <br /> Now, again, just one interpretation, but it does make me view how Seemings and Kiths work somewhat differently, whether 1e or 2e. Its why I view them always having a purpose, albeit an extremely shallow one, for kidnapping people, as an example. <br /> <br /> On another note, I see Seemings as what you were willing to give up to escape, rather than as an expression of agency. While the latter is there... its more as a symptom of personal growth. Hence, why I liked the Darklings as is, because they fit that narrative pretty well. If viewed primarily as an expression of agency, yes, the write-up isn't as good, but, I would argue that isn't the only, or even necessarily dominant, part of being a Seeming.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1657-killer300","name":"Killer300","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"216"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-04T16:50:03-07:00","id":503623,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/498162-second-edition-darklings?p=503530#post503530\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Living embodyment of narrative, sure.<br /> <br /> But even when we're talking about human drama. Anyone can talk to an abuse victim, because an abuse victim is another human. But the abuse victim's life story, if it got up and started walking.<br /> <br /> Sure you can understand the life story, you can look at the individual charchters and understand them as people. You can look at the events and understand them. You can even understand how it all fits togeather.<br /> <br /> But how do you have a <i>conversation</i> with that life story? What does the life story <i>want</i>? What would <i>offend</i> it? Trying to relate to someone's life story, or any story, like it was a person isn't as far out there as interacting with an Abyssal Intruder. But it's close.<br /> <br /> <br /> So - if you're abducted and abused, or abducted and enslaved, by a story. I wouldn't expect the dynamic to resemble human - human abuse.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you're abducted and abused by a story about abduction and abuse (presumably of a human, by a human), then yeah, I expect the dynamic to follow the same general trends as human - human abuse. I mean, a human only figuratively objectifies another human, whereas a Keeper literally transforms them into an actual object. But a metaphor isn't nearly as powerful if it isn't true to reality, at least in structure if not in form.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/498162-second-edition-darklings?p=503530#post503530\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> No that's what I've been saying all along.<br /> <br /> The thing is; to me encouraging would require several options being given equal weight. Either you'd have two more Background and Escape sections for each Seeming at a large wordcount epansion; or you would need to redesign the entire layout to fit several examples in the same wordcount. Which is why I've been suggesting a different layout.</div> </div> </div> </div>I just don't think it needs to be totally re-structured or massively added to to accomplish the goal of encouraging more diversity. Add a few &quot;For some, this might take the form of X, Y, or even Z&quot; here and there to addend the example story, maybe a sidebar near the beginning or end of the section saying something like, &quot;While the stories described here are common of characters of the various seemings, they are by no means the only way the only way it ever plays out. Each individual has their own unique experiences, both in human life and in Arcadia. Feel free to use these examples to inspire your own stories.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/498162-second-edition-darklings?p=503530#post503530\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's a fair question - why would I do that?<br /> <br /> Because like you say, &quot;it doesn't discourage it, but it doesn't encourage it either&quot;. I overlook the qualifiers, because the impression it gives to me is the impression you'd get sans qualifiers.<br /> <br /> Heck; the word &quot;most&quot; is an anti-qualifier. It says they're exceptions but theose exceptions are rare. I might go so far to say the use of the word &quot;most&quot; is explicitly discouraging diversity.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Most&quot; only discourages diversity if you don't want your character to deviate from what is common or typical. Honestly, if you're going to consciously ignore the fact that the writeup goes out of its way to point out that it's only one example among many possibilities, and then complain that it doesn't leave room for other possibilities, that's a problem of your own creation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-04T17:00:21-07:00","id":503628,"title":"","content":"Hey, causal reminder that the game is now broadened out from abuse survivors to trauma survivors. Lara Croft may now apply.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-04T17:00:34-07:00","id":503629,"title":"","content":"@ Charlaquin; Okay. Just scrolling through three to four pages of argument going over the same bits over and over again got wearing for me.<br /> <br /> Anyway;<br /> <br /> For me I don't actually portray the Gentry as spiteful, I go for a more sociopathic viewpoint where they barely understand emotions at all.<br /> <br /> In my games, they very much are the children that never grew up to me too, selfish and incapable to empathizing with others, though it is what they just are and how they think, rather than any choice involved. They take interest in things and then drop them just as easily when something shinier comes along or different. Many changelings in my games haven't been chased up on because of this and that makes the Winter Courtier's extreme paranoia all the more tragic. They are not creative and so they find amusement that is not genuine in things they enjoy but in things they think they should enjoy or what may be in trend or cool. Eventually they may bore of it and find a new game to play. They are creatures of obsession from boredom rather than interest and to me the horror comes from how absolutely blaze they live their existances and the absolute zero thought they give to the actions of which they do that are disturbing at the mild end and flat out sadistic without taking any enjoyment from it at the most terrible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3951-wander","name":"wander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"409"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-04T17:11:55-07:00","id":503637,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/498162-second-edition-darklings?p=503628#post503628\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hey, causal reminder that the game is now broadened out from abuse survivors to trauma survivors. Lara Croft may now apply.</div> </div> </div> </div>Good point, thank you!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-04T17:16:34-07:00","id":503641,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/498162-second-edition-darklings?p=503628#post503628\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hey, causal reminder that the game is now broadened out from abuse survivors to trauma survivors. Lara Croft may now apply.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you. This is an important note.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-04T17:24:35-07:00","id":503644,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/498162-second-edition-darklings?p=503496#post503496\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think you're thinking of the Gentry too much like humans. The gentry have reasons, but often ones that make no sense from a human perspective. There's only so much an understadning of human abuse dynamics can do when you're thinking about the guy who got turned into a painting or a pillar of fire.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is true, but I think there's another angle I also missed until a moment ago. The Gentry's &quot;reason&quot; isn't really covered by Seeming so much as it is by Kith. The general Kith header specified that turning someone into a member of a particular Kith depended in some way on traits that character already possessed, which would be one thing the Gentry could seek out. The Kith helps explain part of <i>why</i> the Gentry took the character. The bit in the Seeming background instead highlights a point of vulnerability in the character: it's a likely avenue for <i>how</i> the Gentry got some hooks in.<br /> <br /> That said, while they are powerfully written and evocative, I generally would like to see the Seeming writeups broadened a bit. I understand and respect reasons for wanting to avoid making them too broad and feel those should be factored in heavily, but, well... Yeah, they kinda do read a bit narrow to me right now. I'm sure that seeing more example Changelings will help me see the ways in which they have more breadth than they currently come across to me -- I am and have always been greatly helped by extensive numbers of examples -- but I'd feel a little constrained at the moment.<br /> <br /> Perhaps putting additional emphasis on the moment of the Escape could be a way to help? Background is helpful to get the mind ticking on a way to set up and support a character's arc and to give the Escape a certain significance, but if there can be said to be a single defining factor for a Seeming, the defining nature of that Escape is the biggie.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/498162-second-edition-darklings?p=503509#post503509\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why would you do that? Those qualifiers are written into the text. If you're going to intentionally overlook parts of the text, don't criticize it for the absence of those parts. They're there, stop overlooking them.</div> </div> </div> </div>To an extent, I can kinda sympathize with The King's Raven here. I mean, I read the writeups. I saw and read the qualifiers, but -- for whatever reason -- I couldn't make myself <i>believe</i> them, if that makes any sense. I'm kind of confused about and trying to dissect that reaction right now, but there it is.<br /> <br /> Perhaps I really am just used to writeups with more examples. Having more ideas of what's common helps me triangulate outward and get a better handle on the spirit of it, from which I'm very comfortable making my own. By contrast, this writeup gives me just the one in-depth example. With the way my mind works, other possibilities just don't spring to mind as easily. As such, I read it as academic fact that there are other sorts of ways a Seeming's story could proceed, but I don't feel grounded enough to clearly identify some of what they actually are, so they don't feel real to me. The brief snippet Concepts at the end aren't helpful on this front, because they're giving me destinations. Interesting destinations, to be sure, but it's alternative journeys I want to help me make one of my own. I don't think there's really wordcount enough for that, though, so... I don't know what to suggest.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/498162-second-edition-darklings?p=503623#post503623\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just don't think it needs to be totally re-structured or massively added to to accomplish the goal of encouraging more diversity. Add a few &quot;For some, this might take the form of X, Y, or even Z&quot; here and there to addend the example story, maybe a sidebar near the beginning or end of the section saying something like, &quot;While the stories described here are common of characters of the various seemings, they are by no means the only way the only way it ever plays out. Each individual has their own unique experiences, both in human life and in Arcadia. Feel free to use these examples to inspire your own stories.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>While part of me might prefer a restructuring, I recognize that part is overreacting. I think listing some alternatives like that would be great, and likely enough to make me happy. The, &quot;These are examples,&quot; lead-in/sidebar might also help with framing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-05T00:50:00-07:00","id":503907,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/498162-second-edition-darklings?p=503623#post503623\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you're abducted and abused by a story about abduction and abuse (presumably of a human, by a human), then yeah, I expect the dynamic to follow the same general trends as human - human abuse. I mean, a human only figuratively objectifies another human, whereas a Keeper literally transforms them into an actual object. But a metaphor isn't nearly as powerful if it isn't true to reality, at least in structure if not in form.</div> </div> </div> </div> I guess we'll have to disagree.<br /> <br /> I think people relate to stories in a different way than they relate to other people - and that would mean the human-keeper dynamic is different than a human-human dynamic.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/498162-second-edition-darklings?p=503623#post503623\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Add a few &quot;For some, this might take the form of X, Y, or even Z&quot; here and there to addend the example story, maybe a sidebar near the beginning or end of the section saying something like, &quot;While the stories described here are common of characters of the various seemings, they are by no means the only way the only way it ever plays out. Each individual has their own unique experiences, both in human life and in Arcadia. Feel free to use these examples to inspire your own stories.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div> I don't see that as enough:<br /> <br /> For some, &quot;abandonment&quot; might take the form of X, Y, or Z. What about the charachter never felt abandoned?<br /> <br /> To me the issue isn't what the text says, it's the emotional impression the text gives. And the current impression is that most Darlklings have similar backgrounds. Explicitly saying they don't wont be enough to deal with that when 90% of the text still focuses on one particular lifestory. It's a bit like how having a sidebar saying LGBT charachters exist in a setting isn't sufficent to be inclusive, you need actual representation - but with no RL people feeling excluded this time.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/498162-second-edition-darklings?p=503623#post503623\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Most&quot; only discourages diversity if you don't want your character to deviate from what is common or typical.</div> </div> </div> </div> Again, it's not just about my charachter. NPCs matter too.<br /> <br /> If there are 10 Darklings in the Freehold and &quot;most&quot; (7? 8? 9?) of them have very very similar backstories, they were all abducted because they're very loyal people, I would find that boring.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gaius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/498162-second-edition-darklings?p=503644#post503644\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Perhaps putting additional emphasis on the moment of the Escape could be a way to help? Background is helpful to get the mind ticking on a way to set up and support a character's arc and to give the Escape a certain significance, but if there can be said to be a single defining factor for a Seeming, the defining nature of that Escape is the biggie.</div> </div> </div> </div> That's how I'd do it if I wanted to limit the amount of changes.<br /> <br /> I'd drop the background section entirely and either use that word count to give a few different examples of escape.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-05T09:03:00-07:00","id":504226,"title":"","content":"I oppose dropping the background it adds so much to Darklings.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-05T10:08:29-07:00","id":504346,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/498162-second-edition-darklings?p=503907#post503907\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I guess we'll have to disagree.<br /> <br /> I think people relate to stories in a different way than they relate to other people - and that would mean the human-keeper dynamic is different than a human-human dynamic.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair enough. Fortunately the Gentry are able to support many different interpreations.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/498162-second-edition-darklings?p=503907#post503907\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't see that as enough:<br /> <br /> For some, &quot;abandonment&quot; might take the form of X, Y, or Z. What about the charachter never felt abandoned?</div> </div> </div> </div>That character is completely acceptable. Nothing wrong with breaking stereotypes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/498162-second-edition-darklings?p=503907#post503907\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To me the issue isn't what the text says, it's the emotional impression the text gives. And the current impression is that most Darlklings have similar backgrounds. Explicitly saying they don't wont be enough to deal with that when 90% of the text still focuses on one particular lifestory. It's a bit like how having a sidebar saying LGBT charachters exist in a setting isn't sufficent to be inclusive, you need actual representation - but with no RL people feeling excluded this time.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's why more examples would help. My suggestion would be to put short ecamples of other backgrounds, durances, and escapes in the &quot;Concepts&quot; section, instead of just the end results.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/498162-second-edition-darklings?p=503907#post503907\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Again, it's not just about my charachter. NPCs matter too.<br /> <br /> If there are 10 Darklings in the Freehold and &quot;most&quot; (7? 8? 9?) of them have very very similar backstories, they were all abducted because they're very loyal people, I would find that boring.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, first of all, I disagree that it would be boring; they would all have a shared experience and be better able to relate to each other. That said, if you find that boring, don't write them all as having been loyal. Maybe only 2 or 3 of them were very loyal. Maybe 3 or 4 of them were extremely honest. Maybe 2 or 3 of them were too trusting. Maybe they all had very different backgrounds, but each shares 1 or 2 common elements with the others. Maybe they don't even have those common elements, they just all follow the general trend of being much more cynical and pragmatic than they were before their Durance, because they all (for various reasons) had to in order to escape.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/498162-second-edition-darklings?p=503907#post503907\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's how I'd do it if I wanted to limit the amount of changes.<br /> <br /> I'd drop the background section entirely and either use that word count to give a few different examples of escape.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would rather they drop just about anything but the background, because it's the best part (IMO, obviously).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-05T23:45:38-07:00","id":505103,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/498162-second-edition-darklings?p=504346#post504346\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That character is completely acceptable. Nothing wrong with breaking stereotypes.</div> </div> </div> </div> But as you know; I don't think you should need to break stereotypes to do it. This stereotype is far too narrow.<br /> <br /> (But thanks for admitting that the Seeming creates a narrow stereotype)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/498162-second-edition-darklings?p=504346#post504346\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's why more examples would help. My suggestion would be to put short examples of other backgrounds, durances, and escapes in the &quot;Concepts&quot; section, instead of just the end results.</div> </div> </div> </div> Since my goal is to replace the stereotype with a broader one simply having characters that break the stereotype wouldn't be enough.<br /> <br /> Heck, you could just move the Background section to the end of the document, entitle it &quot;Sample Character&quot;. Move the first part of The Escape (up to and including &quot;she decided that no one was going to save her&quot;) to be part of Sample Character. Then just tweak it so it's a bout a named Changeling. Would that work for you?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/498162-second-edition-darklings?p=504346#post504346\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok, first of all, I disagree that it would be boring; they would all have a shared experience and be better able to relate to each other.</div> </div> </div> </div> A storyteller could do interesting things with shared expereicnes, but they'd have to do dedicate time to exploring that similarity and the relationships between the Darklings.<br /> <br /> Diversity is interesting by default - it's more appropriate for every story that isn't about exploring that similarity. Like a story about finding and flushing out Huntsmen.<br /> <br /> That's why I suggest Entitlements for this kind of thing; they're clearly there and easily accessible for a Storyteller who wants them but they make the default diverse, which is better for a wider verity of stories and thus more suited as a default.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 05-06-2015, 03:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-06T07:04:57-07:00","id":505403,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/498162-second-edition-darklings?p=505103#post505103\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> But as you know; I don't think you should need to break stereotypes to do it. This stereotype is far too narrow.<br /> <br /> (But thanks for admitting that the Seeming creates a narrow stereotype)</div> </div> </div> </div>I didn't say it was narrow, but ok...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/498162-second-edition-darklings?p=505103#post505103\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Since my goal is to replace the stereotype with a broader one simply having characters that break the stereotype wouldn't be enough.<br /> <br /> Heck, you could just move the Background section to the end of the document, entitle it &quot;Sample Character&quot;. Move the first part of The Escape (up to &quot;she decided that no one was going to save her&quot;) to be part of Sample Character. Then just tweak it so it's a bout a named Changeling. Would that work for you?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that would be fine with me. I'm surprised it suits your goals, because I don't really see a difference between that and what we have now, besides the order it's presented in. But if that could satisfy both of us, I'm down for it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/498162-second-edition-darklings?p=505103#post505103\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> A storyteller could do interesting things with shared expereicnes, but they'd have to do dedicate time to exploring that similarity and the relationships between the Darklings.<br /> <br /> Diversity is interesting by default - it's more appropriate for every story that isn't about exploring that similarity. Like a story about finding and flushing out Huntsmen.<br /> <br /> That's why I suggest Entitlements for this kind of thing; they're clearly there and easily accessible for a Storyteller who wants them but they make the default diverse, which is better for a wider verity of stories and thus more suited as a default.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't agree with any of that, but at this point we're talking about personal taste anyway.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-06T07:19:00-07:00","id":505429,"title":"","content":"If I'm honest, the subject has been talked around in circles so much that I'm fairly sure it should be dropped. People have made their opinions clear, and after three pages of the conversation no one's really moved. Adding more pages has made it clear nothing's changing. David and Filamena have gotten what they probably will out of the current diaglogue.<br /> <br /> I'd change the tracks onto a different track, but I'm too tired to think of another direction. Maybe later in the day.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https