:0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-06T14:31:07-07:00","id":506087,"title":"","content":"Yeah, sorry for dragging that out for so long, but I am glad we came to a resolution we could agree on. I only hope that some of that discussion will be helpful to the folks making the book. How ever it turns out, I'm ecstatic for Changeling 2e!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-07T18:31:10-07:00","id":507466,"title":"","content":"Darklings, what sort of theme song should they have?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-07T19:18:18-07:00","id":507491,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/498162-second-edition-darklings?p=507466#post507466\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Darklings, what sort of theme song should they have?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Behind Blue Eyes?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-07T21:45:22-07:00","id":507639,"title":"","content":"The first kind of music that came to mind was a slow jazz style. The sort of thing you would hear in a noir setting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Changeling inspired games:<br /> <a href=\"http://elfrowen.deviantart.com/art/Escape-Your-Keeper-An-Adventure-Game-417407858\" target=\"_blank\">Escape Your Keeper - An Adventure Game</a><br /> <a href=\"http://www.philome.la/HBruders/finding-freedom---the-office\" target=\"_blank\">Finding Freedom - The Office</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5720-elfrowen","name":"elfrowen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5720_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-07T22:02:18-07:00","id":507674,"title":"","content":"Oh my god, I just thought of how romance stories would go with Darklings. Talk about bittersweet.<br /> <br /> &quot;I'm losing my mind over you.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-08T13:07:24-07:00","id":508358,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/498162-second-edition-darklings?p=507491#post507491\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Behind Blue Eyes?</div> </div> </div> </div> Good choice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-08T14:45:31-07:00","id":508433,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/498162-second-edition-darklings?p=507466#post507466\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Darklings, what sort of theme song should they have?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=4zLfCnGVeL4\" data-code=\"4zLfCnGVeL4\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/4zLfCnGVeL4/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> You're welcome.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-13T04:20:12-07:00","id":512802,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">\u2022 He\u2019s killed, more than once, in the service of his country, and it feels like there\u2019s always blood on his hands. He sleeps well every night, though, because he\u2019ll put down the bad guys, because no one else will. </span></span></span> </div> </div> </div>This sounds like a Chris Kyle expy. It doesn't fit with the given description for Darklings because he doesn't sound like he's betrayed or been betrayed or has a guilty conscience (&quot;sleeps well every night&quot;). Do Beasts, Ogres, et al have any problem with killing Loyalists and Huntsmen? If you want a character who is darkened and is willing to make the hard choices, how about one who didn't shoot a child approaching his unit, and they were killed by a hidden ied?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1460-tau-neutrino","name":"Tau Neutrino","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1460_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-26T11:35:13-07:00","id":529049,"title":"","content":"EH, didn't really like it. It sounded like a Darkling is Batman - loyal, wounded, hiding in shadows, avenging from the darkness. To be fair, that's something that could be a Darkling from the first edition, but the prior-vision of the Darkling was so much broader: antiquarians don't fit into this mold, for instance, nor do several of the other kiths, including my prior character who spent his durance being food for his Master's giant-spiders and was slowly transforming into a type of vampiric fae.<br /> <br /> Just a thought.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3780-nero42","name":"nero42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3780_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-26T11:43:02-07:00","id":529057,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nero42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/498162-second-edition-darklings?p=529049#post529049\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">EH, didn't really like it. It sounded like a Darkling is Batman - loyal, wounded, hiding in shadows, avenging from the darkness. To be fair, that's something that could be a Darkling from the first edition, but the prior-vision of the Darkling was so much broader: antiquarians don't fit into this mold, for instance, nor do several of the other kiths, including my prior character who spent his durance being food for his Master's giant-spiders and was slowly transforming into a type of vampiric fae.<br /> <br /> Just a thought.</div> </div> </div> </div>Under the 2e paradigm, that character might be a different Seeming. Remember, Kith is not tied to Seeming in 2e.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-26T12:00:28-07:00","id":529085,"title":"","content":"oh. didn't know that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3780-nero42","name":"nero42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3780_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-26T13:49:41-07:00","id":529242,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nero42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/498162-second-edition-darklings?p=529085#post529085\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">oh. didn't know that.</div> </div> </div> </div>No worries. There's a lot of changes to keep up with. Basically, the new idea is that Kith is how your Keeper changed you in your Durance. So, a character who was taken to look after a True Fae's museum of curiosities might become an Antiquarian. A character who was taken to be put on display might become a Manequin. A character who was kept in an aquarium might become a Swimmerskin, etc. Your Seeming is how you changed yourself in order to escape. A character who turned wild to escape her cage might become a Beast. A character who turned his back on his previous ideals to do escape no matter the cost might become a Darkling. A character who took charge and lead others to rebel against their captors might become a Fairest, etc. Your Seeming also &quot;flavors&quot; your Kith, so a Swimmerskin Beast may be a fish-person, while a Swimmerskin Darkling may look more like the creature from the black lagoon, and a Swimmerskin Fairest might resemble tales of beautiful mer-people.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-26T14:08:16-07:00","id":529258,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/498162-second-edition-darklings?p=529242#post529242\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No worries. There's a lot of changes to keep up with. Basically, the new idea is that Kith is how your Keeper changed you in your Durance. So, a character who was taken to look after a True Fae's museum of curiosities might become an Antiquarian. A character who was taken to be put on display might become a Manequin. A character who was kept in an aquarium might become a Swimmerskin, etc. Your Seeming is how you changed yourself in order to escape. A character who turned wild to escape her cage might become a Beast. A character who turned his back on his previous ideals to do escape no matter the cost might become a Darkling. A character who took charge and lead others to rebel against their captors might become a Fairest, etc. Your Seeming also &quot;flavors&quot; your Kith, so a Swimmerskin Beast may be a fish-person, while a Swimmerskin Darkling may look more like the creature from the black lagoon, and a Swimmerskin Fairest might resemble tales of beautiful mer-people.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wonder how this'll affect the stereotype perspective in Freeholds...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>nWoD Warhammer Fantasy RPG,<br /> WoD Wraith: The Oblivion<br /> and Infernum-style Demon: The Descent, Shadows of Abaddon --&gt; <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php/topic,26.0.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://madnessforums.com/forums/inde...opic,26.0.html</a><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","name":"MrParaduo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar974_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"967"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-26T14:23:20-07:00","id":529267,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrParaduo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/498162-second-edition-darklings?p=529258#post529258\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wonder how this'll affect the stereotype perspective in Freeholds...</div> </div> </div> </div>Probably become hardliners in some ways, completely evaporate in others. A Beast is literally a Beast because they cheerfully gave both barrels to social convention at some point, so the idea of them being hyper-pragmatic and rude is going to be accepted as a basic fact of life...but not them being savages, because the social system they broke is that of <i>Faerie.</i><br /> <br /> Something tells me a lot of the courts are going to look askance at Darklings, though-they got out through betrayal and regret after all. It's still probably a sign someone's a bit of a bigot if the prejudice is institutionalized, though; they did break out <i>through regret over their actions.</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-26T14:30:34-07:00","id":529275,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrParaduo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/498162-second-edition-darklings?p=529258#post529258\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wonder how this'll affect the stereotype perspective in Freeholds...</div> </div> </div> </div>It'll likely be different than 1e, for sure. The possibility of being Seemingless alone would shape things. Then there's the wrinkle Dave mentioned in another thread that it's not always obvious which Seeming a character has (or whether the character has a Seeming at all). A tiger-guy made of fire may not make for easy stereotyping along Seeming lines.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-26T14:54:15-07:00","id":529299,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/498162-second-edition-darklings?p=529267#post529267\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Probably become hardliners in some ways, completely evaporate in others. A Beast is literally a Beast because they cheerfully gave both barrels to social convention at some point, so the idea of them being hyper-pragmatic and rude is going to be accepted as a basic fact of life...but not them being savages, because the social system they broke is that of <i>Faerie.</i><br /> <br /> Something tells me a lot of the courts are going to look askance at Darklings, though-they got out through betrayal and regret after all. It's still probably a sign someone's a bit of a bigot if the prejudice is institutionalized, though; they did break out <i>through regret over their actions.</i></div> </div> </div> </div>And there's still the possibility it's only their <i>perceived</i> action. Perhaps the darkling only <i>thought</i> he did something worth regretting. Or the beast <i>believed</i> he was going against social convention. Perspective can be just as important as facts when it comes to the dream logic of the Fae.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>nWoD Warhammer Fantasy RPG,<br /> WoD Wraith: The Oblivion<br /> and Infernum-style Demon: The Descent, Shadows of Abaddon --&gt; <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php/topic,26.0.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://madnessforums.com/forums/inde...opic,26.0.html</a><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","name":"MrParaduo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar974_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"967"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-26T16:56:13-07:00","id":529408,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/498162-second-edition-darklings?p=529242#post529242\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No worries. There's a lot of changes to keep up with. Basically, the new idea is that Kith is how your Keeper changed you in your Durance. So, a character who was taken to look after a True Fae's museum of curiosities might become an Antiquarian. A character who was taken to be put on display might become a Manequin. A character who was kept in an aquarium might become a Swimmerskin, etc. Your Seeming is how you changed yourself in order to escape. A character who turned wild to escape her cage might become a Beast. A character who turned his back on his previous ideals to do escape no matter the cost might become a Darkling. A character who took charge and lead others to rebel against their captors might become a Fairest, etc. Your Seeming also &quot;flavors&quot; your Kith, so a Swimmerskin Beast may be a fish-person, while a Swimmerskin Darkling may look more like the creature from the black lagoon, and a Swimmerskin Fairest might resemble tales of beautiful mer-people.</div> </div> </div> </div>confused. might recover if given a few days to process.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3780-nero42","name":"nero42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3780_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-26T17:00:25-07:00","id":529410,"title":"","content":"And it depends on how far you stretch the betrayal perspective. I can imagine a changeling who becomes a darkling because they didn't help everyone else escape with them, and they view their lack of action as a betrayal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Changeling inspired games:<br /> <a href=\"http://elfrowen.deviantart.com/art/Escape-Your-Keeper-An-Adventure-Game-417407858\" target=\"_blank\">Escape Your Keeper - An Adventure Game</a><br /> <a href=\"http://www.philome.la/HBruders/finding-freedom---the-office\" target=\"_blank\">Finding Freedom - The Office</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5720-elfrowen","name":"elfrowen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5720_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-26T17:24:14-07:00","id":529425,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nero42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/498162-second-edition-darklings?p=529408#post529408\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">confused. might recover if given a few days to process.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a bit of a conceptual departure from 1e, no question. It might help to look up <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/category/worlds/worldofdarkness/changelingthelost/\" target=\"_blank\">the previous 2e C:tL blog posts</a> to help ground yourself. In particular, <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/changeling-the-lost-second-edition-beasts/\" target=\"_blank\">the Beast preview</a> gives a short intro to how the process works before describing the Seeming itself, and <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/changeling-the-lost-second-edition-kiths/\" target=\"_blank\">the Kiths preview</a> gives some more detail in its intro as well as a few examples of possible Seeming appearances for each. The latter also teases around a third of the Kiths the final book will have, and those previewed have been pretty damn awesome. ^_^","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-25T04:30:25-07:00","id":567636,"title":"","content":"I wonder what minor curse Darklings will have, perhaps a penalty when out in daylight?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-08T13:08:32-07:00","id":620436,"title":"","content":"I find it lacking that &quot;Darklings&quot; don't have an innate ability to see in the dark.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4045-princeofcincinnati","name":"princeofcincinnati","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4045_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-08T13:23:30-07:00","id":620449,"title":"","content":"Your sense of literalism is duly noted.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}